in the organization.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_device_management_device_enrollment_notification":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"assignments":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"group_id":{"type":"string","description":"The Entra ID group ID to include or exclude in the assignment. Required when type is 'groupAssignmentTarget'.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"type":{"type":"string","description":"Type of assignment target. Must be one of: 'allLicensedUsersAssignmentTarget', 'groupAssignmentTarget'.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"Assignments for the compliance policy. Each assignment specifies the target group and schedule for script execution.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"branding_options":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"The branding options for the message template. Possible values are: none, includeCompanyLogo, includeCompanyName, includeContactInformation, includeCompanyPortalLink, includeDeviceDetails. Defaults to ['none'].","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"default_locale":{"type":"string","description":"The default locale for the notification configuration (e.g., 'en-US').","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"description":{"type":"string","description":"Optional description of the resource. Maximum length is 1500 characters.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"device_enrollment_configuration_type":{"type":"string","description":"The type of device enrollment configuration.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"The display name for the device enrollment notification configuration.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier for the device enrollment notification configuration.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"localized_notification_messages":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"is_default":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether this is the default notification message.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"locale":{"type":"string","description":"The locale for the notification message (e.g., 'en-us'). Must be in lowercase format.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"message_template":{"type":"string","description":"The template content of the notification message.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"subject":{"type":"string","description":"The subject of the notification message.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"template_type":{"type":"string","description":"The type of template (email or push).","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"The localized notification messages for the configuration.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"notification_templates":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"The notification template types for this configuration. Can be 'email', 'push', or both. Defaults to ['email', 'push'].","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"platform_type":{"type":"string","description":"The platform type for the notification configuration. Must be either 'ios', 'windows', 'android', 'androidForWork', 'mac', 'linux'.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"priority":{"type":"number","description":"The priority of the notification configuration.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"role_scope_tag_ids":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"Set of scope tag IDs for this Android Enterprise Notification configuration.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"Manages device enrollment notification configurations using the `/deviceManagement/deviceEnrollmentConfigurations` endpoint. This resource is used to creates device enrollment notification configurations for Android for Work platform.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_device_management_endpoint_privilege_management_json":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"assignments":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"filter_id":{"type":"string","description":"ID of the filter to apply to the assignment. Required when filter_type is 'include' or 'exclude'. Should be omitted when filter_type is 'none'.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"filter_type":{"type":"string","description":"Type of filter to apply. Must be one of: 'include', 'exclude', or 'none'.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"group_id":{"type":"string","description":"The Entra ID group ID to include or exclude in the assignment. Required when type is 'groupAssignmentTarget' or 'exclusionGroupAssignmentTarget'.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"type":{"type":"string","description":"Type of assignment target. Must be one of: 'allDevicesAssignmentTarget', 'allLicensedUsersAssignmentTarget', 'groupAssignmentTarget', 'exclusionGroupAssignmentTarget'.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"Assignments for the device configuration. Each assignment specifies the target group and schedule for script execution. Supports group filters.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"created_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"Creation date and time of the settings catalog policy","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"description":{"type":"string","description":"Optional description of the resource. Maximum length is 1500 characters.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier for this Endpoint Privilege Management Policy","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"is_assigned":{"type":"bool","description":"Indicates if the policy is assigned to any scope","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"last_modified_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"Last modification date and time of the settings catalog policy","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"name":{"type":"string","description":"Policy name","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"platforms":{"type":"string","description":"Platform type for this Endpoint Privilege Management Policy.Will always be set to `windows10`, as EPM currently only supports windows device types.Defaults to windows10.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"role_scope_tag_ids":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"Set of scope tag IDs for this Settings Catalog template profile.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"settings":{"type":"string","description":"Endpoint Privilege Management Policy settings defined as a JSON string. Please provide a valid JSON-encoded settings structure. This can either be extracted from an existing policy using the Intune gui `export JSON` functionality if supported, via a script such as this powershell script. [Export-IntuneSettingsCatalogConfigurationById](https://github.com/deploymenttheory/terraform-provider-microsoft365/blob/main/scripts/device_management/Export-IntuneSettingsCatalogConfigurationById.ps1) or created from scratch. The JSON structure should match the graph schema of the settings catalog. Please look at the terraform documentation for the Endpoint Privilege Management Policy for examples and how to correctly format the HCL.\n\nA correctly formatted field in the HCL should begin and end like this:\n```hcl\nsettings = jsonencode({\n  \"settings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"0\",\n      \"settingInstance\": {\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n})\n```\n\n**Note:** Settings must always be provided as an array within the settings field, even when configuring a single setting.This is required because the Microsoft Graph SDK for Go always returns settings in an array format\n\n**Note:** When configuring secret values (identified by @odata.type: \"#microsoft.graph.deviceManagementConfigurationSecretSettingValue\") ensure the valueState is set to \"notEncrypted\". The value \"encryptedValueToken\" is reserved for serverresponses and should not be used when creating or updating settings.\n\n```hcl\nsettings = jsonencode({\n  \"settings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"0\",\n      \"settingInstance\": {\n        \"@odata.type\": \"#microsoft.graph.deviceManagementConfigurationSimpleSettingInstance\",\n        \"settingDefinitionId\": \"com.apple.loginwindow_autologinpassword\",\n        \"settingInstanceTemplateReference\": null,\n        \"simpleSettingValue\": {\n          \"@odata.type\": \"#microsoft.graph.deviceManagementConfigurationSecretSettingValue\",\n          \"valueState\": \"notEncrypted\",\n          \"value\": \"your_secret_value\",\n          \"settingValueTemplateReference\": null\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n})\n```\n\nAlternatively, if you prefer a fully hcl based approach, you can use the resource `microsoft365_graph_beta_device_management_settings_catalog_configuration_policy` by creating the epm policy via thr gui and then exporting the settings catalog configuration to hcl using the [Export-IntuneSettingsCatalogConfigurationToHCL.ps1] (https://github.com/deploymenttheory/terraform-provider-microsoft365/blob/main/scripts/device_management/Export-IntuneSettingsCatalogConfigurationToHCL.ps1) script.This will create a fully hcl based epm policy with all the settings catalog settings configured.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"settings_catalog_template_type":{"type":"string","description":"Defines which Endpoint Privilege Management Policy type with settings catalog setting will be deployed. Options available are `elevation_settings_policy` or `elevation_rules_policy`.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"settings_count":{"type":"number","description":"Number of settings catalog settings with the policy. This will change over time as the resource is updated.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"technologies":{"type":["list","string"],"description":"Describes a list of technologies this Endpoint Privilege Management Policy with settings catalog setting will be deployed with.Defaults to `mdm`, `endpointPrivilegeManagement`.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"Manages Endpoint Privilege Management policies using the `/deviceManagement/configurationPolicies` endpoint. This resource is used to ePM policies control elevation settings and rules for Windows devices, allowing administrators to grant temporary administrative privileges to standard users for specific applications or processes without compromising overall security posture.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_device_management_group_policy_configuration":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"assignments":{"nested_type":{"attribu