efinitions configured for this policy. Possible values are: unknown, custom, builtIn, mixed, unknownFutureValue","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"role_scope_tag_ids":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"Set of scope tag IDs for this Group Policy Configuration.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"Manages group policy configurations using the `/deviceManagement/groupPolicyConfigurations` endpoint. This resource is used to the group policy configuration entity contains the configured values for one or more group policy definitions.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_device_management_group_policy_definition":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"category_path":{"type":"string","description":"The category path of the group policy definition (e.g., '\\Windows Components\\App Package Deployment'). Used to identify the policy in the catalog","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"class_type":{"type":"string","description":"The class type of the group policy definition. Must be 'user' or 'machine'","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"created_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time when the definition value was created","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"enabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether this group policy definition is enabled (true) or disabled (false)","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"group_policy_configuration_id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier of the group policy configuration that contains this definition","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier for the group policy definition value","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"last_modified_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time when the definition value was last modified","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"policy_name":{"type":"string","description":"The display name of the group policy definition (e.g., 'Remove Default Microsoft Store packages from the system.')","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"values":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier of the presentation template (computed from catalog)","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"label":{"type":"string","description":"The human-readable label of the presentation (e.g., 'Xbox Gaming App', 'Feedback Hub'). Must match a label from the policy's catalog definition","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"value":{"type":"string","description":"The value for this presentation as a string. Format depends on presentation type: 'true'/'false' for checkboxes, numeric strings for decimal fields, plain text for textboxes, etc. The resource validates and converts this based on the presentation type","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"Set of presentation values for this group policy definition. Each value corresponds to a specific presentation (checkbox, textbox, dropdown, etc.) identified by its label. The resource automatically handles type conversion based on the presentation type in the catalog.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true}},"description":"Manages a group policy definition with all its presentation values in Microsoft Intune. This resource provides a unified interface for configuring any group policy regardless of presentation types (checkboxes, textboxes, dropdowns, etc.). Values are provided as label-value pairs, and the resource automatically handles type conversion based on the policy's catalog definition. Uses the `deviceManagement/groupPolicyConfigurations('{groupPolicyConfigurationId}')/updateDefinitionValues` endpoint.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_device_management_group_policy_uploaded_definition_files":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"content":{"type":"string","description":"The content of the group policy uploaded definition file. Request is sent as raw bytes. This is a write-only field and will not be stored in state.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"default_language_code":{"type":"string","description":"The default language code of the group policy uploaded definition file. Must be in the format 'xx-YY' (e.g., 'en-US', 'fr-FR').","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"description":{"type":"string","description":"Optional description of the resource. Maximum length is 1500 characters.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"The display name of the group policy uploaded definition file.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"file_name":{"type":"string","description":"The file name of the group policy uploaded definition file.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"force_definition_file_upload":{"type":"bool","description":"If set to true, any existing definition file with the same target namespace will be deleted before uploading the new file. This is useful when re-uploading ADMX files that may already exist in the tenant. Defaults to false.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"group_policy_uploaded_language_files":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"content":{"type":"string","description":"The content of the group policy uploaded language file. Request is sent as raw bytes. This is a write-only field and will not be stored in state.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"file_name":{"type":"string","description":"The file name of the group policy uploaded language file.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"language_code":{"type":"string","description":"The language code of the group policy uploaded language file. Must be in the format 'xx-YY' (e.g., 'en-US', 'fr-FR').","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"The language file(s) associated with the group policy uploaded definition file.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the group policy uploaded definition file.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"language_codes":{"type":["list","string"],"description":"The language codes supported by the group policy uploaded definition file.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"last_modified_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time when the group policy uploaded definition file was last modified.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"policy_type":{"type":"string","description":"The policy type of the group policy uploaded definition file.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"revision":{"type":"string","description":"The revision of the group policy uploaded definition file.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"status":{"type":"string","description":"The status of the group policy uploaded definition file. Possible values are: uploadInProgress, available, uploadFailed.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"target_namespace":{"type":"string","description":"The target namespace of the group policy uploaded definition file.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"target_prefix":{"type":"string","description":"The target prefix of the group policy uploaded definition file.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"upload_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time when the group policy uploaded definition file was uploaded.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"description":"Manages group policy uploaded definition files using the `/deviceManagement/groupPolicyUploadedDefinitionFiles` endpoint. This resource is used to group policy uploaded definition files are ADMX files that define group policies that can be deployed to devices.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_device_management_intune_branding_profile":{"version":1,"block":{"attributes":{"assignments":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"group_id":{"type":"string","description":"The Entra ID group ID to include or exclude in the assignment. Required when type is 'groupAssignmentTarget' or 'exclusionGroupAssignmentTarget'.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"type":{"type":"string","description":"Type of assignment target. Must be one of: 'allDevicesAssignmentTarget', 'allLicensedUsersAssignmentTarget', 'groupAssignmentTarget', 'exclusionGroupAssignmentTarget'.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"Assignments for the Windows remediation script. Each assignment specifies the target group and schedule for script execution.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"company_portal_blocked_actions":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"action":{"type":"string","description":"Action to block. Possible values are: `unknown`, `remove`, `reset`.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"owner_type":{"type":"string","description":"Device ownership type. Possible values are: `unknown`, `company`, `personal`.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"platform":{"type":"string","description":"Device platform. Possible values are: `android`, `androidForWork`, `iOS`, `macOS`, `windowsPhone81`, `windows81AndLater`, `windows10AndLater`, `androidWorkProfile`, `unknown`, `androidAOSP`, `androidMobileApplicationManagement`, `iOSMobileApplicationManagement`, `unknownFutureValue`, `windowsMobileApplicationManagement`.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"Collection of blocked actions on the company portal as per platform and device ownership types.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"contact_it_email_address":{"type":"string","description":"Email address of the person/organization responsible for IT support.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"contact_it_name":{"type":"string","description":"Name of the person/organization responsible for IT support.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"contact_it_notes":{"type":"string","description":"Text comments regarding the person/organization responsible for IT support.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"contact_it_phone_number":{"type":"string","description":"Phone number of the person/organization responsible for IT support.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"created_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"Time when the BrandingProfile was created.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"custom_can_see_privacy_message":{"type":"string","description":"Text comments regarding what the admin can see on the device.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"custom_cant_see_privacy_message":{"type":"string","description":"Text comments regarding what the admin can't see on the device.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"custom_privacy_message":{"type":"string","description":"Text comments regarding what the admin has access to on the device.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"disable_client_telemetry":{"type":"bool","description":"Applies to telemetry sent from all clients to the Intune service. When disabled, all proactive troubleshooting and issue warnings within the client are turned off, and telemetry settings appear grayed out or hidden to the device user.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"disable_device_category_selection":{"type":"bool","description":"Boolean that indicates if device category selection is disabled during enrollment.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"Company/organization name that is displayed to end users.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"enrollment_availability":{"type":"string","description":"Customized device enrollment flow displayed to the end user. Possible values are: `availableWithPrompts`, `availableWithoutPrompts`, `unavailable`.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier for the branding profile.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"is_default_profile":{"type":"bool","description":"Boolean that represents whether the profile is used as default or not.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"is_factory_reset_disabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Boolean that represents whether the adminstrator has disabled the 'Factory Reset' action on corporate owned devices.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"is_remove_device_disabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Boolean that represents whether the adminstrator has disabled the 'Remove Device' action on corporate owned devices.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"landing_page_customized_image":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"image_file_path_source":{"type":"string","description":"The file path to the image file to be uploaded. Supports various image formats.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"image_url_source":{"type":"string","description":"The web location of the image file, can be a http(s) URL. Supports various image formats.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Customized image displayed in Company Portal app landing page. Supports various image formats which will be automatically converted as required by Microsoft Intune.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"last_modified_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"Time when the BrandingProfile was last modified.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"light_background_logo":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"image_file_path_source":{"type":"string","description":"The file path to the image file to be uploaded. Supports various image formats.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"image_url_source":{"type":"string","description":"The web location of the image file, can be a http(s) URL. Supports various image formats.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Logo image displayed in Company Portal apps which have a light background behind the logo. Supports various image formats which will be automatically converted as required by Microsoft Intune.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"online_support_site_name":{"type":"string","description":"Display name of the company/organization's IT helpdesk site.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"online_support_site_url":{"type":"string","description":"URL to the company/organization's IT helpdesk site.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"privacy_url":{"type":"string","description":"URL to the company/organization's privacy policy.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"profile_description":{"type":"string","description":"Description of the branding profile.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"profile_name":{"type":"string","description":"Name of the branding profile.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"role_scope_tag_ids":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"Set of scope tag IDs for this Settings Catalog template profile.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"send_device_ownership_change_push_notification":{"type":"bool","description":"Boolean that indicates if a push notification is sent to users when their device ownership type changes from personal to corporate.","description_kind":"markdown","deprecated":true,"deprecation_message":"sendDeviceOwnershipChangePushNotification was removed from the Microsoft Graph beta API in msgraph-beta-sdk-go v0.160.0. This field no longer has any effect and will be removed in a future provider version. Remove it from your configuration.","optional":true,"computed":true},"show_azure_ad_enterprise_apps":{"type":"bool","description":"Boolean that indicates if AzureAD Enterprise Apps will be shown in Company Portal.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"show_configuration_manager_apps":{"type":"bool","description":"Boolean that indicates if Configuration Manager Apps will be shown in Company Portal.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"show_display_name_next_to_logo":{"type":"bool","description":"Boolean that represents whether the administrator-supplied display name text is shown next to the logo image or not.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"show_logo":{"type":"bool","description":"Boolean that represents whether the administrator-supplied logo images are shown or not.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"show_office_web_apps":{"type":"bool","description":"Boolean that indicates if Office WebApps will be shown in Company Portal.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"theme_color":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"b":{"type":"number","description":"Blue value (0-255).","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"g":{"type":"number","description":"Green value (0-255).","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"r":{"type":"number","description":"Red value (0-255).","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Primary theme color used in the Company Portal applications and web portal.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"theme_color_logo":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"image_file_path_source":{"type":"string","description":"The file path to the image file to be uploaded. Supports various image formats.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"image_url_source":{"type":"string","description":"The web location of the image file, can be a http(s) URL. Supports various image formats.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Logo image displayed in Company Portal apps which have a theme color background behind the logo. Supports various image formats which will be automatically converted as required by Microsoft Intune.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"Manages an Intune branding profile resource in Intune.\n\n## API Documentation\n\n- [Graph API Endpoint](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/graph/api/resources/intune-wip-intunebrandingprofile?view=graph-rest-beta)","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_device_management_ios_device_compliance_policy":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"advanced_threat_protection_required_security_level":{"type":"string","description":"Require Microsoft Defender for Endpoint minimum risk level to report noncompliance. Possible values are: unavailable, secured, low, medium, high, notSet","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"assignments":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"filter_id":{"type":"string","description":"ID of the filter to apply to the assignment.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"filter_type":{"type":"string","description":"Type of filter to apply. Must be one of: 'include', 'exclude', or 'none'.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"group_id":{"type":"string","description":"The Entra ID group ID to include or exclude in the assignment. Required when type is 'groupAssignmentTarget' or 'exclusionGroupAssignmentTarget'.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"type":{"type":"string","description":"Type of assignment target. Must be one of: 'allDevicesAssignmentTarget', 'allLicensedUsersAssignmentTarget', 'groupAssignmentTarget', 'exclusionGroupAssignmentTarget'.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"Assignments for the compliance policy. Each assignment specifies the target group and schedule for script execution.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"description":{"type":"string","description":"Optional description of the resource. Maximum length is 1500 characters.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"device_threat_protection_enabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Require that devices have enabled device threat protection","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"device_threat_protection_required_security_level":{"type":"string","description":"Require Device Threat Protection minimum risk level to report noncompliance. Possible values are: unavailable, secured, low, medium, high, notSet","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"The display name of the device compliance policy","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The id of the driver.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"managed_email_profile_required":{"type":"bool","description":"Indicates whether or not to require a managed email profile","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"os_maximum_build_version":{"type":"string","description":"Maximum iOS build version","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"os_maximum_version":{"type":"string","description":"Maximum iOS version allowed.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"os_minimum_build_version":{"type":"string","description":"Minimum iOS build version","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"os_minimum_version":{"type":"string","description":"Minimum iOS version allowed.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"passcode_block_simple":{"type":"bool","description":"Indicates whether or not to block simple passcodes","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"passcode_expiration_days":{"type":"number","description":"Number of days before the passcode expires. Valid values 1 to 65535","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"passcode_minimum_character_set_count":{"type":"number","description":"The number of character sets required in the password","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"passcode_minimum_length":{"type":"number","description":"Minimum length of passcode. Valid values 4 to 14","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"passcode_minutes_of_inactivity_before_lock":{"type":"number","description":"Minutes of inactivity before a passcode is required","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"passcode_minutes_of_inactivity_before_screen_timeout":{"type":"number","description":"Minutes of inactivity before the screen times out","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"passcode_previous_passcode_block_count":{"type":"number","description":"Number of previous passwords to block","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"passcode_required":{"type":"bool","description":"Indicates whether or not to require a passcode","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"passcode_required_type":{"type":"string","description":"The required passcode type. Possible values are: deviceDefault, alphanumeric, numeric","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"restricted_apps":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"app_id":{"type":"string","description":"The application or bundle identifier of the application","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"app_store_url":{"type":"string","description":"The Store URL of the application","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"name":{"type":"string","description":"The application name","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"publisher":{"type":"string","description":"The publisher of the application","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"Require the device to not have the specified apps installed. This collection can contain a maximum of 100 elements","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"role_scope_tag_ids":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"Set of scope tag IDs for this Entity instance.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"scheduled_actions_for_rule":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"rule_name":{"type":"string","description":"Name of the scheduled action rule","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"scheduled_action_configurations":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"action_type":{"type":"string","description":"What action to take. Possible values are: 'noAction', 'notification', 'block', 'retire', 'wipe', 'removeResourceAccessProfiles', 'pushNotification', 'remoteLock'.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"grace_period_hours":{"type":"number","description":"Number of hours to wait till the action will be enforced","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"notification_message_cc_list":{"type":["list","string"],"description":"A list of group GUIDs to specify who to CC this notification message to","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"notification_template_id":{"type":"string","description":"What notification Message template to use","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"The list of scheduled action configurations for this compliance policy","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"list"},"description":"The list of scheduled action for this rule","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"security_block_jailbroken_devices":{"type":"bool","description":"Indicates the device should not be jailbroken. When TRUE, if the device is detected as jailbroken it will be reported non-compliant","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"Manages ios device compliance policies using the `/deviceManagement/deviceCompliancePolicies` endpoint. This resource is used to device compliance policies define rules and settings that devices must meet to be considered compliant with organizational security requirements.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_device_management_ios_ipados_device_enrollment_policy":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"action_button_screen_disabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether to hide the configuration pane for the action button in Setup Assistant. For iOS/iPadOS 17.0 and later.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"app_store_disabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether to hide the Apple App Store pane in Setup Assistant. For iOS/iPadOS 14.3 and later.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"appearance_screen_disabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether to hide the appearance setup pane in Setup Assistant. For iOS/iPadOS 13.0 and later.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"apple_id_disabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether to hide the Apple ID setup pane in Setup Assistant, which gives users the option to sign in with their Apple ID and use iCloud. For iOS/iPadOS 7.0 and later.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"apple_intelligence_disabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether to hide the Apple Intelligence setup pane in Setup Assistant, where users can configure Apple Intelligence features. For iOS/iPadOS 18.0 and later.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"apple_pay_disabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether to hide the Apple Pay setup pane in Setup Assistant, which gives users the option to set up Apple Pay on their devices. For iOS/iPadOS 7.0 and later.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"await_final_configuration":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether devices are locked in Setup Assistant until all enrollment-time configuration is installed (await final configuration). Only applicable when `require_setup_assistant_with_modern_authentication` is `true`.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"camera_button_screen_disabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether to hide the camera button pane in Setup Assistant. For iOS/iPadOS 18.0 and later.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"cellular_data_activation_url":{"type":"string","description":"The carrier activation server URL used to activate cellular data plans on eligible devices at enrollment. When omitted, cellular data plan activation is not configured by this profile.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"created_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"Creation date and time of the policy.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"dep_onboarding_settings_id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the Apple ABM/ASM DEP onboarding token (`/deviceManagement/depOnboardingSettings`) that owns this profile. If omitted, it is automatically resolved to the tenant's single Apple ADE/ABM (or ASM) token; if the tenant has more than one Apple token, this must be set explicitly.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"description":{"type":"string","description":"Optional description of the resource. Maximum length is 1500 characters.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"device_name_template":{"type":"string","description":"Device name template applied to supervised devices at enrollment, e.g. `{{DEVICETYPE}}-{{SERIAL}}`. Supports the `{{DEVICETYPE}}` and `{{SERIAL}}` substitution tokens. When omitted, device naming is not managed by this profile.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"device_security_group":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the static Microsoft Entra security group to use for enrollment time grouping (the \"Device group\" tab in the Intune admin center policy wizard). Devices assigned this policy become members of the group as they enroll. This is set via the dedicated `setEnrollmentTimeDeviceMembershipTarget` action on `/deviceManagement/configurationPolicies/{id}` (and cleared via `clearEnrollmentTimeDeviceMembershipTarget` when removed), not via the settings catalog. The group must have the 'Intune Provisioning Client' service principal (AppId: f1346770-5b25-470b-88bd-d5744ab7952c) set as its owner; in some tenants this service principal may appear as 'Intune Autopilot ConfidentialClient'.\n\n~\u003e **Known Microsoft Graph limitation:** as of this writing, `setEnrollmentTimeDeviceMembershipTarget` and `clearEnrollmentTimeDeviceMembershipTarget` return an `Internal Server Error - 500` from the Intune backend (`DeviceConfigV2`) when called with application permissions (client credentials) - the auth flow this provider always uses. The identical request succeeds when made with delegated (signed-in user) permissions, e.g. from the Intune admin center. Until Microsoft resolves this for application permissions, setting `device_security_group` through this provider will fail on `Create` and `Update`; this is a Microsoft Graph service limitation, not a provider defect.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"device_to_device_migration_disabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether to hide the device-to-device migration pane in Setup Assistant. When shown, users can transfer data from an old device to their current device. The option to transfer data directly from a device isn't available for devices running iOS 13 or later.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"diagnostics_disabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether to hide the diagnostics pane in Setup Assistant, where users can opt in to send diagnostic data to Apple. For iOS/iPadOS 7.0 and later.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"enable_authentication_via_company_portal":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether the user authenticates via the Company Portal app instead of Setup Assistant. Only applicable when `requires_user_authentication` is `true`. Mutually exclusive with `require_setup_assistant_with_modern_authentication`.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"get_started_screen_disabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether to hide the Get Started pane in Setup Assistant.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier for this policy.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"imessage_and_facetime_disabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether to hide the iMessage and FaceTime setup pane in Setup Assistant. For iOS/iPadOS 9.0 and later.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"is_assigned":{"type":"bool","description":"Indicates if the policy is assigned to any scope.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"is_default_policy_assignment":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether this policy is the default iOS/iPadOS enrollment profile for its `dep_onboarding_settings_id`, set via the dedicated `setDefaultProfile` action. Always reflects the DEP token's actual current default on refresh, regardless of configuration.\n\n~\u003e **No unassign action:** Microsoft Graph does not expose an `unsetDefaultProfile`/`clearDefaultProfile` action - `setDefaultProfile` is the only operation available. Setting this to `false` on a policy that is currently the DEP token's default has no effect on Graph; the next refresh reports `true` again. Only setting a different policy's `is_default_policy_assignment` to `true` changes which profile is the default. A change from `true` to `false` while this policy is still the token's current default can therefore never converge, and the provider rejects the update with a validation error. Promote the replacement policy first - in the same apply, give this policy a `depends_on` for the replacement so the promotion runs first, or apply the promotion separately.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"last_modified_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"Last modification date and time of the policy.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"location_services_disabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether to hide the Location Services setup pane in Setup Assistant, where users can enable location services on their device. For iOS/iPadOS 7.0 and later.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"lockdown_mode_disabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether to hide the Lockdown Mode pane in Setup Assistant.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"locked_enrollment_enabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether enrollment is locked to the authorized user/device, preventing the MDM profile from being removed before enrollment completes.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"multitasking_screen_disabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether to hide the multitasking pane in Setup Assistant. For iOS/iPadOS 26.0 and later.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"name":{"type":"string","description":"The display name of the enrollment profile.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"os_showcase_screen_disabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether to hide the OS showcase pane in Setup Assistant. For iOS/iPadOS 26.0 and later.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"passcode_disabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether to hide the passcode and password lock pane in Setup Assistant. When shown, users are prompted for a passcode. Always require a passcode for unsecured devices unless access is controlled in some other way (such as through a kiosk mode configuration that restricts the device to one app). For iOS/iPadOS 7.0 and later.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"platforms":{"type":"string","description":"The platforms this policy applies to. Always `iOS`.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"privacy_pane_disabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether to hide the privacy setup pane in Setup Assistant. For iOS/iPadOS 11.3 and later.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"require_setup_assistant_with_modern_authentication":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether the user authenticates in Setup Assistant using modern authentication (Microsoft Entra ID). Only applicable when `requires_user_authentication` is `true`. Mutually exclusive with `enable_authentication_via_company_portal`.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"requires_user_authentication":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether the enrollment requires user authentication (user affinity). When `false`, the device enrolls without an associated user (shared/kiosk device path). When `true`, the authentication flow is selected via `enable_authentication_via_company_portal` or `require_setup_assistant_with_modern_authentication`; when neither is set, the legacy Setup Assistant authentication flow is used.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"restore_completed_screen_disabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether to hide the Restore Completed screen shown after a backup and restore is performed during Setup Assistant.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"restore_disabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether to hide the apps and data (Restore) setup pane in Setup Assistant. When shown, users setting up devices can restore or transfer data from iCloud Backup. For iOS/iPadOS 7.0 and later.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"restore_from_android_disabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether to hide the Android Migration setup pane in Setup Assistant, meant for previous Android users. When shown, users can migrate data from an Android device. For iOS/iPadOS 9.0 and later.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"role_scope_tag_ids":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"Set of scope tag IDs for this Settings Catalog template profile.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"safety_and_handling_screen_disabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether to hide the safety and handling pane in Setup Assistant. For iOS/iPadOS 18.4 and later.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"safety_screen_disabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether to hide the safety (Emergency SOS) setup pane in Setup Assistant. For iOS/iPadOS 16.0 and later.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"screen_time_screen_disabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether to hide the Screen Time pane in Setup Assistant. For iOS/iPadOS 12.0 and later.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"settings_count":{"type":"number","description":"Number of settings within the policy.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"sim_setup_screen_disabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether to hide the cellular (SIM Setup) pane in Setup Assistant, where users can add a cellular plan. For iOS/iPadOS 12.0 and later.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"siri_disabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether to hide the Siri setup pane in Setup Assistant. For iOS/iPadOS 7.0 and later.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"software_update_completed_screen_disabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether to hide the screen showing all software updates that happen during Setup Assistant.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"software_update_screen_disabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether to hide the mandatory software update screen in Setup Assistant. For iOS/iPadOS 12.0 and later.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"support_department":{"type":"string","description":"The department name shown to the user on the Setup Assistant Remote Management pane. Must be between 1 and 125 characters.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"support_phone_number":{"type":"string","description":"The support phone number shown to the user on the Setup Assistant Remote Management pane. Must be between 1 and 50 characters.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"technologies":{"type":"string","description":"The technology this policy is using. Always `enrollment`.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"template_family":{"type":"string","description":"The template family for this policy (`enrollmentConfiguration`).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"template_id":{"type":"string","description":"The settings catalog template ID used by this policy.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"terms_and_conditions_disabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether to hide the Apple terms and conditions pane in Setup Assistant. When shown, users are required to accept them. For iOS/iPadOS 7.0 and later.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"terms_of_address_screen_disabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether to hide the terms of address pane in Setup Assistant, which gives users the option to choose how they want to be addressed throughout the system: feminine, masculine, or neutral. This Apple feature is available for select languages. For iOS/iPadOS 16.0 and later.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"touch_id_disabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether to hide the biometric (Touch ID and Face ID) setup pane in Setup Assistant, which gives users the option to set up fingerprint or facial identification on their devices. For iOS/iPadOS 8.1 and later.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"watch_migration_screen_disabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether to hide the Apple Watch migration pane in Setup Assistant, where users can migrate data from an Apple Watch. For iOS/iPadOS 11.0 and later.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"web_content_filtering_disabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether to hide the web content filtering pane in Setup Assistant. For iOS/iPadOS 18.2 and later.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true}},"description":"Manages an iOS/iPadOS Automated Device Enrollment (ADE) profile using the `/deviceManagement/configurationPolicies` settings catalog endpoint. This is the modern, settings-catalog-backed equivalent of the legacy `depIOSEnrollmentProfile` API, and controls iOS/iPadOS Setup Assistant behavior for devices enrolled via Apple Business Manager / Apple School Manager.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_device_management_linux_device_compliance_policy":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"assignments":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"filter_id":{"type":"string","description":"ID of the filter to apply to the assignment.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"filter_type":{"type":"string","description":"Type of filter to apply. Must be one of: 'include', 'exclude', or 'none'.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"group_id":{"type":"string","description":"The Entra ID group ID to include or exclude in the assignment. Required when type is 'groupAssignmentTarget' or 'exclusionGroupAssignmentTarget'.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"type":{"type":"string","description":"Type of assignment target. Must be one of: 'allDevicesAssignmentTarget', 'allLicensedUsersAssignmentTarget', 'groupAssignmentTarget', 'exclusionGroupAssignmentTarget'.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"Assignments for the compliance policy. Each assignment specifies the target group and schedule for script execution.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"created_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"Date and time when the Linux device compliance policy was created.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"custom_compliance_discovery_script":{"type":"string","description":"Reference ID to the custom compliance discovery script for Linux devices.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"custom_compliance_required":{"type":"bool","description":"Indicates whether custom compliance rules are required for Linux devices.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"custom_compliance_rules":{"type":"string","description":"Base64-encoded JSON string containing custom compliance rules for Linux devices.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"description":{"type":"string","description":"Optional description of the resource. Maximum length is 1500 characters.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"device_encryption_required":{"type":"bool","description":"Indicates whether device encryption is required for Linux devices to be considered compliant.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"distribution_allowed_distros":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"maximum_version":{"type":"string","description":"Maximum version of the Linux distribution that is considered compliant.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"minimum_version":{"type":"string","description":"Minimum version of the Linux distribution that is considered compliant.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"type":{"type":"string","description":"Type of Linux distribution (e.g., 'ubuntu', 'rhel', 'centos', 'debian', 'suse').","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"list"},"description":"List of allowed Linux distributions with version constraints.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"Unique identifier for the Linux device compliance policy.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"is_assigned":{"type":"bool","description":"Indicates whether this Linux device compliance policy is assigned to any groups.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"last_modified_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"Date and time when the Linux device compliance policy was last modified.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"name":{"type":"string","description":"Name of the Linux device compliance policy.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"password_policy_minimum_digits":{"type":"number","description":"Minimum number of digit characters required in the Linux device password.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"password_policy_minimum_length":{"type":"number","description":"Minimum length required for the Linux device password.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"password_policy_minimum_lowercase":{"type":"number","description":"Minimum number of lowercase characters required in the Linux device password.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"password_policy_minimum_symbols":{"type":"number","description":"Minimum number of symbol characters required in the Linux device password.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"password_policy_minimum_uppercase":{"type":"number","description":"Minimum number of uppercase characters required in the Linux device password.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"platforms":{"type":"string","description":"Platform for which this policy applies. Always 'linux' for Linux device compliance policies.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"role_scope_tag_ids":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"List of Scope Tags for this Linux device compliance policy instance.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"scheduled_actions":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"rule_name":{"type":"string","description":"Name of the scheduled action rule. always use 'PasswordRequired' for Linux device compliance policies","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"scheduled_action_configurations":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"action_type":{"type":"string","description":"What action to take. Possible values are: 'noAction', 'notification', 'block', 'retire', 'wipe', 'removeResourceAccessProfiles', 'pushNotification', 'remoteLock'.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"grace_period_hours":{"type":"number","description":"Number of hours to wait till the action will be enforced","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"notification_message_cc_list":{"type":["list","string"],"description":"A list of group GUIDs to specify who to CC this notification message to","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"notification_template_id":{"type":"string","description":"What notification Message template to use","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"The list of scheduled action configurations for this compliance policy","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"list"},"description":"The list of scheduled action for this rule","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"settings_count":{"type":"number","description":"Number of settings configured in this Linux device compliance policy.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"technologies":{"type":"string","description":"Technology stack for the policy. Always 'linuxMdm' for Linux device compliance policies.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"Manages Linux device compliance policies using the `/deviceManagement/configurationPolicies` endpoint. This resource is used to linux device compliance policies define rules and settings that Linux devices must meet to be considered compliant with organizational security requirements. These policies use the Settings Catalog configuration framework to provide granular control over Linux device compliance settings..","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_device_management_linux_device_compliance_script":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"description":{"type":"string","description":"Optional description of the resource. Maximum length is 1500 characters.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"detection_script_content":{"type":"string","description":"The entire content of the detection shell script for Linux compliance checking.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"Name of the Linux device compliance script.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"Unique identifier for the Linux device compliance script.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"last_modified_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The timestamp of when the Linux device compliance script was modified. This property is read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"setting_definition_id":{"type":"string","description":"The setting definition ID for Linux custom compliance discovery script.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"version":{"type":"number","description":"Version of the Linux device compliance script.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"description":"Manages Linux device compliance scripts using the `/deviceManagement/reusablePolicySettings` endpoint. This resource is used to linux device compliance scripts enable running shell scripts on enrolled Linux devices to validate compliance requirements and provide custom compliance assessments.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_device_management_linux_platform_script":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"assignments":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"filter_id":{"type":"string","description":"ID of the filter to apply to the assignment. Required when filter_type is 'include' or 'exclude'. Should be omitted when filter_type is 'none'.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"filter_type":{"type":"string","description":"Type of filter to apply. Must be one of: 'include', 'exclude', or 'none'.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"group_id":{"type":"string","description":"The Entra ID group ID to include or exclude in the assignment. Required when type is 'groupAssignmentTarget' or 'exclusionGroupAssignmentTarget'.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"type":{"type":"string","description":"Type of assignment target. Must be one of: 'allDevicesAssignmentTarget', 'allLicensedUsersAssignmentTarget', 'groupAssignmentTarget', 'exclusionGroupAssignmentTarget'.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"Assignments for the device configuration. Each assignment specifies the target group and schedule for script execution. Supports group filters.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"description":{"type":"string","description":"Optional description of the resource. Maximum length is 1500 characters.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"execution_context":{"type":"string","description":"Execution context for the linux platform script. Can be one of: user or root. Defaults to user.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"execution_frequency":{"type":"string","description":"Execution frequency for the Linux platform script. Can be one of: `15minutes`, `30minutes`, `1hour`, `2hour`, `3hour`, `6hour`, `12hour`, `1day`, or `1week`. Defaults to `15minutes`.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"execution_retries":{"type":"string","description":"Number of times the Linux platform script should be retried on failure. Can be one of: `1`, `2`, or `3`. Defaults to `1`.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier of the linux platform script.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"name":{"type":"string","description":"Name of the linux device management script.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"platforms":{"type":"string","description":"Platform type for this linux platform script.Will always be set to ['linux'],unknownFutureValue, androidEnterprise, or aosp. Defaults to none.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"role_scope_tag_ids":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"Set of scope tag IDs for this Settings Catalog template profile.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"script_content":{"type":"string","description":"The linux script content. This will be base64 encoded as part of the request.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true,"sensitive":true},"technologies":{"type":["list","string"],"description":"Describes the technologies this settings catalog setting can be deployed with. Defaults to ['linuxMdm'].","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"Manages Linux platform scripts using the `/deviceManagement/configurationPolicies` endpoint. This resource is used to linux platform scripts enable automated deployment and execution of shell scripts on managed Linux devices with configurable execution contexts, retry logic, and scheduled execution frequencies for system administration and maintenance tasks.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_device_management_macos_custom_attribute_script":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"assignments":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"group_id":{"type":"string","description":"The Entra ID group ID to include or exclude in the assignment. Required when type is 'groupAssignmentTarget' or 'exclusionGroupAssignmentTarget'.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"type":{"type":"string","description":"Type of assignment target. Must be one of: 'allDevicesAssignmentTarget', 'allLicensedUsersAssignmentTarget', 'groupAssignmentTarget', 'exclusionGroupAssignmentTarget'.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"Assignments for the Windows remediation script. Each assignment specifies the target group and schedule for script execution.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":tr