ting can be deployed with. Valid values are: `none`, `mdm`, `windows10XManagement`, `configManager`, `intuneManagementExtension`, `thirdParty`, `documentGateway`, `appleRemoteManagement`, `microsoftSense`, `exchangeOnline`, `mobileApplicationManagement`, `linuxMdm`, `enrollment`, `endpointPrivilegeManagement`, `unknownFutureValue`, `windowsOsRecovery`, and `android`. Defaults to `mdm`.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"template_reference":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"template_display_name":{"type":"string","description":"Template Display Name of the referenced template. This property is read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"template_display_version":{"type":"string","description":"Template Display Version of the referenced Template. This property is read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"template_family":{"type":"string","description":"Describes the TemplateFamily for the Template entity. This is a read-only property.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"template_id":{"type":"string","description":"Template ID to reference. This is a UUID that identifies a specific template in Microsoft Intune.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Policy template reference information","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"Manages Intune Settings Catalog policies using the `/deviceManagement/configurationPolicies` endpoint. This resource is used to settings Catalog provides a unified configuration experience for Windows, macOS, iOS/iPadOS, and Android devices through a modern, simplified interface that replaces traditional device configuration profiles and legacy Intune configuration templates. You can simplify the hcl creation process by using the `Export-IntuneSettingsCatalogConfigurationToHCL.ps1` [https://github.com/deploymenttheory/terraform-provider-microsoft365/blob/main/scripts/powershell/device_management/Export-IntuneSettingsCatalogConfigurationToHCL.ps1] script to export the settings catalog and settings catalog templates.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_device_management_settings_catalog_configuration_policy_json":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"assignments":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"filter_id":{"type":"string","description":"Filter identity. Include/exclude requires a non-zero GUID. An explicit zero GUID is supported only with none (also the default mode).","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"filter_type":{"type":"string","description":"Type of filter to apply. Must be one of: 'include', 'exclude', or 'none'.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"group_id":{"type":"string","description":"The Entra ID group ID to include or exclude in the assignment. Required when type is 'groupAssignmentTarget' or 'exclusionGroupAssignmentTarget'.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"type":{"type":"string","description":"Type of assignment target. Must be one of: 'allDevicesAssignmentTarget', 'allLicensedUsersAssignmentTarget', 'groupAssignmentTarget', 'exclusionGroupAssignmentTarget'.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"Assignments for the device configuration. Each assignment specifies the target group and schedule for script execution. Supports group filters.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"created_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"Creation date and time of the settings catalog policy","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"description":{"type":"string","description":"Optional description of the resource. Maximum length is 1500 characters.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier for this policy","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"is_assigned":{"type":"bool","description":"Indicates if the policy is assigned to any scope","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"last_modified_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"Last modification date and time of the settings catalog policy","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"name":{"type":"string","description":"Policy name","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"platforms":{"type":"string","description":"Platform type for this settings catalog policy.Can be one of: `none`, `android`, `iOS`, `macOS`, `windows10X`, `windows10`, `linux`,`unknownFutureValue`, `androidEnterprise`, or `aosp`. Defaults to `none`.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"role_scope_tag_ids":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"Set of scope tag IDs for this Entity instance.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"settings":{"type":"string","description":"Settings Catalog Policy template settings defined as a JSON string. Please provide a valid JSON-encoded settings structure. This can either be extracted from an existing policy using the Intune gui `export JSON` functionality if supported, via a script such as this powershell script. [ExportSettingsCatalogConfigurationById](https://github.com/deploymenttheory/terraform-provider-microsoft365/blob/main/scripts/powershell/Export-IntuneSettingsCatalogConfigurationById.ps1) or created from scratch. The JSON structure should match the graph schema of the settings catalog. Please look at the terraform documentation for the settings catalog template for examples and how to correctly format the HCL.\n\nA correctly formatted field in the HCL should begin and end like this:\n```hcl\nsettings = jsonencode({\n  \"settings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"0\",\n      \"settingInstance\": {\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n})\n```\n\n**Note:** Settings must always be provided as an array within the settings field, even when configuring a single setting.This is required because the Microsoft Graph SDK for Go always returns settings in an array format\n\n**Note:** When configuring secret values (identified by @odata.type: \"#microsoft.graph.deviceManagementConfigurationSecretSettingValue\") ensure the valueState is set to \"notEncrypted\". The value \"encryptedValueToken\" is reserved for serverresponses and should not be used when creating or updating settings.\n\n```hcl\nsettings = jsonencode({\n  \"settings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"0\",\n      \"settingInstance\": {\n        \"@odata.type\": \"#microsoft.graph.deviceManagementConfigurationSimpleSettingInstance\",\n        \"settingDefinitionId\": \"com.apple.loginwindow_autologinpassword\",\n        \"settingInstanceTemplateReference\": null,\n        \"simpleSettingValue\": {\n          \"@odata.type\": \"#microsoft.graph.deviceManagementConfigurationSecretSettingValue\",\n          \"valueState\": \"notEncrypted\",\n          \"value\": \"your_secret_value\",\n          \"settingValueTemplateReference\": null\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n})\n```\n\n","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"settings_catalog_template_type":{"type":"string","description":"Defines which settings catalog setting template will be deployed. Unused by non settings catalog template items, but required in schema to satisify tfsdk model.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"settings_count":{"type":"number","description":"Number of settings catalog settings with the policy. This will change over time as the resource is updated.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"technologies":{"type":["list","string"],"description":"Describes a list of technologies this settings catalog setting can be deployed with. Valid values are: `none`, `mdm`, `windows10XManagement`, `configManager`, `intuneManagementExtension`, `thirdParty`, `documentGateway`, `appleRemoteManagement`, `microsoftSense`, `exchangeOnline`, `mobileApplicationManagement`, `linuxMdm`, `enrollment`, `endpointPrivilegeManagement`, `unknownFutureValue`, `windowsOsRecovery`, and `android`. Defaults to `mdm`.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"Manages a Settings Catalog policy in Microsoft Intune for Windows, macOS, iOS/iPadOS and Android.","description_kind":"plain"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_device_management_settings_catalog_inventory_policy":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"assignments":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"filter_id":{"type":"string","description":"ID of the filter to apply to the assignment. Required when filter_type is 'include' or 'exclude'. Should be omitted when filter_type is 'none'.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"filter_type":{"type":"string","description":"Type of filter to apply. Must be one of: 'include', 'exclude', or 'none'.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"group_id":{"type":"string","description":"The Entra ID group ID to include or exclude in the assignment. Required when type is 'groupAssignmentTarget' or 'exclusionGroupAssignmentTarget'.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"type":{"type":"string","description":"Type of assignment target. Must be one of: 'allDevicesAssignmentTarget', 'allLicensedUsersAssignmentTarget', 'groupAssignmentTarget', 'exclusionGroupAssignmentTarget'.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"Assignments for the device configuration. Each assignment specifies the target group and schedule for script execution. Supports group filters.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"configuration_policy":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"settings":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"id":{"type":"string","description":"Key of this setting within the policy which contains it. Automatically generated.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true,"computed":true},"setting_instance":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"choice_setting_collection_value":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"children":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"odata_type":{"type":"string","description":"OData type identifier","description_kind":"plain","required":true},"setting_definition_id":{"type":"string","description":"Setting definition identifier","description_kind":"plain","required":true},"setting_instance_template_reference":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"setting_instance_template_id":{"type":"string","description":"Setting instance template identifier","description_kind":"plain","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Template reference at instance level","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"simple_setting_collection_value":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"odata_type":{"type":"string","description":"OData type identifier","description_kind":"plain","required":true},"setting_value_template_reference":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"setting_value_template_id":{"type":"string","description":"Setting va