ntifier for the web filtering policy rule.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"name":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the web filtering rule.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"priority":{"type":"number","description":"The rule priority. Lower numbers are evaluated before higher numbers. The Entra portal accepts values from 100 to 65000.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"session_types":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"Session types that must match the rule. Possible values are `user` and `agent`.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"status":{"type":"string","description":"The rule status. Possible values are `enabled` and `disabled`.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"urls_or_fqdns":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"URL or FQDN destination patterns for the rule, for example `www.MySite.com`, `www.MySite.com/a/b/c`, `www.MySite.com/a/*`, or `*.mysite.com`. Use `*` to match any URL or FQDN. At least one of `urls_or_fqdns` or `web_categories` must be specified; both can be set on the same rule. If set, this attribute must contain at least one value. The Entra portal shows URL/FQDN destinations as comma-separated text, while Microsoft Graph stores them as a values array; Terraform follows the Graph shape with one set element per destination.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"web_categories":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"Web category IDs for the rule, for example `AlcoholAndTobacco`. At least one of `urls_or_fqdns` or `web_categories` must be specified; both can be set on the same rule. If set, this attribute must contain at least one value. Category IDs are passed through to Microsoft Graph unchanged.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"web_filtering_policy_id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the web filtering policy that owns this rule.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"description":"Manages rules for Microsoft Entra Global Secure Access web filtering policies using the Microsoft Graph beta `/networkaccess/webFilteringPolicies/{id}/policyRules` endpoint observed from the Entra portal.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_m365_admin_browser_site":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"allow_redirect":{"type":"bool","description":"Controls the behavior of redirected sites. If `true`, indicates that the site will open in Internet Explorer 11 or Microsoft Edge even if the site is navigated to as part of a HTTP or meta refresh redirection chain.","description_kind":"plain","required":true},"browser_site_list_assignment_id":{"type":"string","description":"The browser site list id to assign this browser site to.","description_kind":"plain","required":true},"comment":{"type":"string","description":"The comment for the site.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"compatibility_mode":{"type":"string","description":"Controls what compatibility setting is used for specific sites or domains.","description_kind":"plain","required":true},"created_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time when the site was created.","description_kind":"plain","computed":true},"deleted_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time when the site was deleted.","description_kind":"plain","computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier of the browser site.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"last_modified_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time when the site was last modified.","description_kind":"plain","computed":true},"merge_type":{"type":"string","description":"The merge type of the site.","description_kind":"plain","required":true},"status":{"type":"string","description":"Indicates the status of the site.","description_kind":"plain","computed":true},"target_environment":{"type":"string","description":"The target environment that the site should open in.","description_kind":"plain","required":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"web_url":{"type":"string","description":"The URL of the site.","description_kind":"plain","required":true}},"description":"Manages browser sites for Internet Explorer mode using the `/admin/edge/internetExplorerMode/siteLists/{siteListId}/sites` endpoint. This resource is used to configures specific websites to load in Internet Explorer 11 compatibility mode within Microsoft Edge, enabling legacy web application support through controlled compatibility settings.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_m365_admin_browser_site_list":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"description":{"type":"string","description":"Optional description of the resource. Maximum length is 1500 characters.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the site list.","description_kind":"plain","required":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier for the site list.","description_kind":"plain","computed":true},"last_modified_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time when the site list was last modified.","description_kind":"plain","computed":true},"published_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time when the site list was published.","description_kind":"plain","computed":true},"revision":{"type":"string","description":"The current revision of the site list.","description_kind":"plain","computed":true},"status":{"type":"string","description":"The current status of the site list.","description_kind":"plain","computed":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"Manages Internet Explorer mode site lists using the `/admin/edge/internetExplorerMode/siteLists` endpoint. This resource is used to site lists are collections of websites that require Internet Explorer 11 compatibility mode, allowing organizations to maintain legacy web applications while transitioning to Microsoft Edge as the default browser.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_users_user":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"about_me":{"type":"string","description":"A freeform text entry field for users to describe themselves.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"account_enabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Set to `true` if the account is enabled; otherwise, `false`. This property is required when a user is created.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"age_group":{"type":"string","description":"Sets the age group of the user. Allowed values: `null`, `Minor`, `NotAdult`, `Adult`. Refer to the legal age group property definitions for further information.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"business_phones":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"The telephone numbers for the user. NOTE: Although it is a string collection, only one number can be set for this property.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"city":{"type":"string","description":"The city where the user is located. Maximum length is 128 characters.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"company_name":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the company that the user is associated with. This property can be useful for describing the company that an external user comes from. Maximum length is 64 characters.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"consent_provided_for_minor":{"type":"string","description":"Sets whether consent was obtained for minors. Allowed values: `null`, `Granted`, `Denied`, `NotRequired`. Refer to the legal age group property definitions for further information.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"country":{"type":"string","description":"The country or region where the user is located; for example, `US` or `UK`. Maximum length is 128 characters.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"created_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time the user was created, in ISO 8601 format and UTC. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"creation_type":{"type":"string","description":"Indicates whether the user account was created through one of the following methods: As a regular school or work account (`null`), as an external account (`Invitation`), as a local account for an Azure Active Directory B2C tenant (`LocalAccount`), through self-service sign-up by an internal user using email verification (`EmailVerified`), or through self-service sign-up by an external user signing up through a link that is part of a user flow (`SelfServiceSignUp`). Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"custom_security_attributes":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"attribute_set":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the attribute set (e.g., `Engineering`, `Marketing`). This groups related custom security attributes together.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"attributes":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"bool_value":{"type":"bool","description":"The value if the attribute is a boolean type. Exactly one of `string_value`, `int_value`, `bool_value`, `string_values`, or `int_values` must be specified.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"int_value":{"type":"number","description":"The value if the attribute is a single-valued integer type. Exactly one of `string_value`, `int_value`, `bool_value`, `string_values`, or `int_values` must be specified.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"int_values":{"type":["set","number"],"description":"The values if the attribute is a multi-valued integer type. Exactly one of `string_value`, `int_value`, `bool_value`, `string_values`, or `int_values` must be specified.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"name":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the custom security attribute.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"string_value":{"type":"string","description":"The value if the attribute is a single-valued string type. Exactly one of `string_value`, `int_value`, `bool_value`, `string_values`, or `int_values` must be specified.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"string_values":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"The values if the attribute is a multi-valued string type. Exactly one of `string_value`, `int_value`, `bool_value`, `string_values`, or `int_values` must be specified.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"The collection of custom security attributes within this attribute set.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"An open complex type that holds the value of a custom security attribute that is assigned to a directory object. Nullable. Returned only on `$select`. Supports `$filter` (eq, ne, not, startsWith). The filter value is case-sensitive. To read this property, the calling app must be assigned the `CustomSecAttributeAssignment.Read.All` permission. To write this property, the calling app must be assigned the `CustomSecAttributeAssignment.ReadWrite.All` permission.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"deleted_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time the user was deleted. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"department":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the department in which the user works. Maximum length is 64 characters.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"The name displayed in the address book for the user. This is usually the combination of the user's first name, middle initial, and last name. This property is required when a user is created and it cannot be cleared during updates. Maximum length is 256 characters.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"employee_hire_date":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time when the user was hired or will start work in case of a future hire, in ISO 8601 format and UTC.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"employee_id":{"type":"string","description":"The employee identifier assigned to the user by the organization. Maximum length is 16 characters.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"employee_type":{"type":"string","description":"Captures enterprise worker type. For example, `Employee`, `Contractor`, `Consultant`, or `Vendor`.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"external_user_state":{"type":"string","description":"For an external user invited to the tenant using the invitation API, this property represents the invited user's invitation status. For invited users, the state can be `PendingAcceptance` or `Accepted`, or `null` for all other users. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"external_user_state_change_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"Shows the timestamp for the latest change to the externalUserState property. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"fax_number":{"type":"string","description":"The fax number of the user.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"given_name":{"type":"string","description":"The given name (first name) of the user. Maximum length is 64 characters.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"hard_delete":{"type":"bool","description":"When `true`, the user will be permanently deleted (hard delete) during destroy. When `false` (default), the user will only be soft deleted and moved to the deleted items container where it can be restored within 30 days. Note: This field defaults to `false` on import since the API does not return this value.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier for the user. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"job_title":{"type":"string","description":"The user's job title. Maximum length is 128 characters.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"mail":{"type":"string","description":"The SMTP address for the user, for example, `jeff@contoso.com`. Changes to this property also update the user's proxyAddresses collection to include the value as an SMTP address.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"mail_nickname":{"type":"string","description":"The mail alias for the user. This property must be specified when a user is created. Maximum length is 64 characters.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"manager_id":{"type":"string","description":"The user ID of the user's manager. Used to set the organizational hierarchy. To update the manager, provide the user ID of the new manager. To remove the manager, set this to an empty string.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"mobile_phone":{"type":"string","description":"The primary cellular telephone number for the user.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"office_location":{"type":"string","description":"The office location in the user's place of business. Maximum length is 128 characters.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"on_premises_distinguished_name":{"type":"string","description":"Contains the on-premises Active Directory `distinguished name` or `DN`. The property is only populated for customers who are synchronizing their on-premises directory to Microsoft Entra ID via Microsoft Entra Connect. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"on_premises_domain_name":{"type":"string","description":"Contains the on-premises `domainFQDN`, also called dnsDomainName synchronized from the on-premises directory. The property is only populated for customers who are synchronizing their on-premises directory to Microsoft Entra ID via Microsoft Entra Connect. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"on_premises_immutable_id":{"type":"string","description":"This property is used to associate an on-premises Active Directory user account to their Microsoft Entra user object. This property must be specified when creating a new user account in the Graph if you're using a federated domain for the user's userPrincipalName (UPN) property.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"on_premises_last_sync_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"Indicates the last time at which the object was synced with the on-premises directory; for example: `2013-02-16T03:04:54Z`. The Timestamp type represents date and time information using ISO 8601 format and is always in UTC. For example, midnight UTC on Jan 1, 2014 is `2014-01-01T00:00:00Z`. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"on_premises_sam_account_name":{"type":"string","description":"Contains the on-premises `sAMAccountName` synchronized from the on-premises directory. The property is only populated for customers who are synchronizing their on-premises directory to Microsoft Entra ID via Microsoft Entra Connect. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"on_premises_security_identifier":{"type":"string","description":"Contains the on-premises security identifier (SID) for the user that was synchronized from on-premises to the cloud. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"on_premises_sync_enabled":{"type":"bool","description":"`true` if this user object is currently being synced from an on-premises Active Directory (AD); otherwise, the user isn't being synced and can be managed in Microsoft Entra ID. Read-only. The value is `null` for cloud-only users.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"on_premises_user_principal_name":{"type":"string","description":"Contains the on-premises `userPrincipalName` synchronized from the on-premises directory. The property is only populated for customers who are synchronizing their on-premises directory to Microsoft Entra ID via Microsoft Entra Connect. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"other_mails":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"A list of additional email addresses for the user; for example: `[\"bob@contoso.com\", \"Robert@fabrikam.com\"]`. NOTE: This property can't contain accent characters. Maximum length per value is 250 characters.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"password_policies":{"type":"string","description":"Specifies password policies for the user. This value is an enumeration with one possible value being `DisableStrongPassword`, which allows weaker passwords than the default policy to be specified. `DisablePasswordExpiration` can also be specified. The two may be specified together; for example: `DisablePasswordExpiration, DisableStrongPassword`.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"password_profile":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"force_change_password_next_sign_in":{"type":"bool","description":"true if the user must change their password on the next login; otherwise false. This is a write-only field used only for initial provisioning.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true,"write_only":true},"force_change_password_next_sign_in_with_mfa":{"type":"bool","description":"If true, at next sign-in, the user must perform a multi-factor authentication (MFA) before being forced to change their password. The behavior is identical to forceChangePasswordNextSignIn except that the user is required to first perform a multi-factor authentication before password change. This is a write-only field used only for initial provisioning. Defaults to false if not specified.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"write_only":true},"password":{"type":"string","description":"The password for the user. This property is required when a user is created. This is a write-only field used only for initial provisioning - the API never returns password values.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true,"sensitive":true,"write_only":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Specifies the password profile for the user. The profile contains the user's password. This property is required when a user is created. These fields are write-only and used only for initial user provisioning. Password management after user creation should be handled through proper identity management workflows, not Terraform.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"postal_code":{"type":"string","description":"The postal code for the user's postal address. The postal code is specific to the user's country/region. In the United States of America, this attribute contains the ZIP code. Maximum length is 40 characters.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"preferred_data_location":{"type":"string","description":"The preferred data location for the user. For more information, see OneDrive Online Multi-Geo.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"preferred_language":{"type":"string","description":"The preferred language for the user. The preferred language format is based on RFC 4646. The name combines an ISO 639 two-letter lowercase culture code associated with the language and an ISO 3166 two-letter uppercase subculture code associated with the country or region. Example: `en-US`, or `es-ES`.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"preferred_name":{"type":"string","description":"The preferred name for the user. **Not Supported.** This attribute returns an empty string.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"proxy_addresses":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"Email addresses that also represent the user for the same mailbox. For example: `[\"SMTP: bob@contoso.com\", \"smtp: bob@sales.contoso.com\"]`. Changes to the mail property also update this collection to include the value as an SMTP address. For more information, see mail and proxyAddresses properties. The proxy address prefixed with SMTP (capitalized) is the primary proxy address. This property can't contain accent characters. Read-only in Microsoft Graph; you can only update this property through the Microsoft 365 admin center.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"security_identifier":{"type":"string","description":"Security identifier (SID) of the user, used in Windows scenarios. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"show_in_address_list":{"type":"bool","description":"`true` if the Outlook global address list should contain this user, otherwise `false`. If not set, this will be treated as `true`. For users invited through the invitation manager, this property will be set to `false`.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"sign_in_sessions_valid_from_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"Any refresh tokens or sessions tokens (session cookies) issued before this time are invalid, and applications get an error when using an invalid refresh or sessions token to acquire a delegated access token (to access APIs such as Microsoft Graph). If this happens, the application needs to acquire a new refresh token by making a request to the authorize endpoint. Read-only. Use revokeSignInSessions to reset.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"state":{"type":"string","description":"The state or province in the user's address. Maximum length is 128 characters.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"street_address":{"type":"string","description":"The street address of the user's place of business. Maximum length is 1024 characters.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"surname":{"type":"string","description":"The user's surname (family name or last name). Maximum length is 64 characters.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"usage_location":{"type":"string","description":"A two-letter country code (ISO standard 3166). Required for users that are assigned licenses due to legal requirements to check for availability of services in countries. Examples include: `US`, `JP`, and `GB`. Not nullable.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"user_principal_name":{"type":"string","description":"The user principal name (UPN) of the user. The UPN is an Internet-style sign-in name for the user based on the Internet standard RFC 822. By convention, this should map to the user's email name. The general format is alias@domain, where the domain must be present in the tenant's collection of verified domains. This property is required when a user is created. The verified domains for the tenant can be accessed from the verifiedDomains property of organization. NOTE: This property can't contain accent characters. Only the following characters are allowed: A-Z, a-z, 0-9, ' . - _ ! # ^ ~. For the complete list of allowed characters, see username policies.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"user_type":{"type":"string","description":"A string value that can be used to classify user types in your directory, such as `Member` and `Guest`.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true}},"description":"Manages Microsoft 365 users using the `/users` endpoint. This resource is used to the user resource lets admins specify user preferences for languages and date/time formats for the user's primary Exchange mailboxes and Microsoft Entra profile. Permissions for this resource are complex and depend on the specific fields you wish tomanage. For more information, see the Microsoft Documentation. https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/graph/api/user-update?view=graph-rest-beta\u0026tabs=http#permissions-for-specific-scenarios.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_users_user_license_assignment":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"disabled_plans":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"A collection of the unique identifiers for service plans to disable for this license. When omitted from configuration, all plans are enabled (any previously disabled plans are cleared).","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier for this license assignment resource. Format: `{user_id}_{sku_id}`.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"sku_id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier (GUID) for the license SKU to assign to the user.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"user_id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier for the user. Can be either the object ID (UUID) or user principal name (UPN).","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"user_principal_name":{"type":"string","description":"The user principal name (UPN) of the user. This is computed and read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"description":"Manages a single Microsoft 365 license assignment for an individual user using the `/users/{userId}/assignLicense` endpoint. This resource allows management to Add or remove licenses for the user to enable or disable their use of Microsoft cloud offerings that the company has licenses to. For example, an organization can have a Microsoft 365 Enterprise E3 subscription with 100 licenses, and this request assigns one of those licenses to a specific user. You can also enable and disable specific plans associated with a subscription. ","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_users_user_mailbox_settings":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"automatic_replies_setting":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"external_audience":{"type":"string","description":"The audience that will receive external automatic reply messages. Possible values: `none`, `contactsOnly`, `all`.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"external_reply_message":{"type":"string","description":"The automatic reply message to send to external recipients. Supports HTML formatting.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"internal_reply_message":{"type":"string","description":"The automatic reply message to send to internal recipients. Supports HTML formatting.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"scheduled_end_date_time":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time value in ISO 8601 format (e.g., `2026-03-20T02:00:00`). The timezone is specified separately in the `time_zone` field.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"time_zone":{"type":"string","description":"The time zone for the date time value. Defaults to `UTC` if not specified.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"The end date and time when automatic replies are scheduled to stop being sent. Required when status is `scheduled`.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"scheduled_start_date_time":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time value in ISO 8601 format (e.g., `2026-03-19T02:00:00`). The timezone is specified separately in the `time_zone` field.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"time_zone":{"type":"string","description":"The time zone for the date time value. Defaults to `UTC` if not specified.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"The start date and time when automatic replies are scheduled to be sent. Required when status is `scheduled`.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"status":{"type":"string","description":"The status of automatic replies. Possible values: `disabled`, `alwaysEnabled`, `scheduled`.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Configuration for automatic replies (also known as Out of Office or OOF) for the user's mailbox.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"date_format":{"type":"string","description":"The date format for the user's mailbox. This uses [.NET standard date format patterns](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/standard/base-types/standard-date-and-time-format-strings#ShortDate) that are culture-specific. Common values include: `M/d/yyyy` (US), `dd/MM/yyyy` (UK/EU), `yyyy-MM-dd` (ISO), `dd.MM.yyyy` (German). The format determines how dates are displayed in the user's mailbox.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"delegate_meeting_message_delivery_options":{"type":"string","description":"Specifies how meeting messages and responses are delivered to delegates. Possible values: `sendToDelegateAndInformationToPrincipal`, `sendToDelegateAndPrincipal`, `sendToDelegateOnly`.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"Computed identifier for this resource (format: users/{user_id}/mailboxSettings). Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"language":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"The display name of the locale. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"locale":{"type":"string","description":"A locale representation for the user, which includes the user's preferred language and country/region. For example, `en-US`. The language component follows 2-letter codes as defined in [ISO 639-1](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_ISO_639_language_codes), and the country component follows 2-letter codes as defined in [ISO 3166-1 alpha-2](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_3166-1_alpha-2).","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"The locale (language and country/region) information for the user.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"time_format":{"type":"string","description":"The time format for the user's mailbox. This uses [.NET standard time format patterns](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/standard/base-types/standard-date-and-time-format-strings#ShortTime) that are culture-specific. Common examples include: `h:mm tt` (1:45 PM - US 12-hour), `HH:mm` (13:45 - European 24-hour). The format determines how times are displayed in the user's mailbox.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"time_zone":{"type":"string","description":"The default time zone for the user's mailbox. Must be one of the Windows time zone names supported by Microsoft Graph API. Common values include `Pacific Standard Time`, `Eastern Standard Time`, `UTC`, etc. See the [Microsoft Graph API documentation](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/graph/api/outlookuser-supportedtimezones) for the full list of supported time zones.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"user_id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the user whose mailbox settings are being managed. This can be the user's object ID or userPrincipalName.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"user_purpose":{"type":"string","description":"The purpose of the mailbox. Differentiates a mailbox for a single user from a shared mailbox and equipment mailbox in Exchange Online. Possible values are: user, linked, shared, room, equipment, others, unknownFutureValue. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"working_hours":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"days_of_week":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"The days of the week on which the user works. Possible values: `sunday`, `monday`, `tuesday`, `wednesday`, `thursday`, `friday`, `saturday`.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"end_time":{"type":"string","description":"The time the user stops working each day, in HH:mm:ss format (e.g., `17:00:00`).","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"start_time":{"type":"string","description":"The time the user starts working each day, in HH:mm:ss format (e.g., `09:00:00`).","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"time_zone":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"name":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the time zone. Must be one of the supported Windows time zone names (e.g., `Pacific Standard Time`, `Eastern Standard Time`, `UTC`). See the [Microsoft Graph API documentation](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/graph/api/outlookuser-supportedtimezones) for the full list.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"The time zone for the working hours. Must be one of the Windows time zone names supported by Microsoft Graph API.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"The working hours configured for the user's calendar.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true}},"description":"Manages Microsoft 365 user mailbox settings using the `/users/{id}/mailboxSettings` endpoint. This resource is used to allows you to configure automatic replies, date/time formats, locale, time zone, working hours, and other mailbox preferences for a user. Note: This resource manages settings that may also be modified by users through Outlook clients.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_users_user_manager":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier for this user manager relationship. This is the same as user_id.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"manager_id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier (GUID) of the user or organizational contact to assign as the manager.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"user_id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier (GUID) of the user whose manager is being managed.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"description":"Manages the manager relationship for a user in Microsoft Entra ID using the Microsoft Graph Beta API.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_windows_365_azure_network_connection":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"ad_domain_name":{"type":"string","description":"The fully qualified domain name (FQDN) of the Active Directory domain you want to join. Optional.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"ad_domain_password":{"type":"string","description":"The password associated with adDomainUsername.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"sensitive":true},"ad_domain_username":{"type":"string","description":"The username of an Active Directory account (user or service account) that has permissions to create computer objects in Active Directory. Required format: admin@contoso.com. Optional.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"connection_type":{"type":"string","description":"Specifies the method by which a provisioned Cloud PC is joined to Microsoft Entra. The azureADJoin option indicates the absence of an on-premises Active Directory (AD) in the current tenant that results in the Cloud PC device only joining to Microsoft Entra. The hybridAzureADJoin option indicates the presence of an on-premises AD in the current tenant and that the Cloud PC joins both the on-premises AD and Microsoft Entra. The selected option also determines the types of users who can be assigned and can sign into a Cloud PC. The azureADJoin option allows both cloud-only and hybrid users to be assigned and sign in, whereas hybridAzureADJoin is restricted to hybrid users only. Default: hybridAzureADJoin. Possible values: hybridAzureADJoin, azureADJoin, unknownFutureValue.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"The display name for the Azure network connection.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"health_check_status":{"type":"string","description":"The status of the most recent health check done on the Azure network connection. For example, if the status is passed, the Azure network connection passed all checks run by the service. Possible values: pending, running, passed, failed, warning, informational, unknownFutureValue. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"Unique identifier for the Azure network connection. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"in_use":{"type":"bool","description":"Indicates whether a Cloud PC is using this on-premises network connection. true if at least one Cloud PC is using it. Otherwise, false. Read-only. Default is false.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"managed_by":{"type":"string","description":"Specifies which services manage the Azure network connection. Possible values: windows365, devBox, unknownFutureValue, rpaBox. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"organizational_unit":{"type":"string","description":"The organizational unit (OU) in which the computer account is created. If left null, the OU configured as the default (a well-known computer object container) in your Active Directory domain (OU) is used. Optional.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"resource_group_id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the target resource group. Required format: /subscriptions/{subscriptionId}/resourceGroups/{resourceGroupName}.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"subnet_id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the target subnet. Required format: /subscriptions/{subscriptionId}/resourceGroups/{resourceGroupName}/providers/Microsoft.Network/virtualNetworks/{virtualNetworkId}/subnets/{subnetName}.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"subscription_id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the target Azure subscription associated with your tenant.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"virtual_network_id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the target virtual network. Required format: /subscriptions/{subscriptionId}/resourceGroups/{resourceGroupName}/providers/Microsoft.Network/virtualNetworks/{virtualNetworkName}.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"description_kind":"plain"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_windows_365_cloud_pc_alert_rule":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"alert_rule_template":{"type":"string","description":"The rule template of the alert event. Possible values: cloudPcProvisionScenario, cloudPcImageUploadScenario, cloudPcOnPremiseNetworkConnectionCheckScenario, unknownFutureValue, cloudPcInGracePeriodScenario, cloudPcFrontlineInsufficientLicensesScenario, cloudPcInaccessibleScenario, cloudPcFrontlineConcurrencyScenario.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"conditions":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"aggregation":{"type":"string","description":"The built-in aggregation method for the rule condition. Possible values: count, percentage, affectedCloudPcCount, affectedCloudPcPercentage, unknownFutureValue, durationInMinutes.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"condition_category":{"type":"string","description":"The property that the rule condition monitors. Possible values: provisionFailures, imageUploadFailures, azureNetworkConnectionCheckFailures, cloudPcInGracePeriod, frontlineInsufficientLicenses, cloudPcConnectionErrors, cloudPcHostHealthCheckFailures, cloudPcZoneOutage, unknownFutureValue, frontlineBufferUsageDuration, frontlineBufferUsageThreshold.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"operator":{"type":"string","description":"The built-in operator for the rule condition. Possible values: greaterOrEqual, equal, greater, less, lessOrEqual, notEqual, unknownFutureValue.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"relationship_type":{"type":"string","description":"The relationship type. Possible values: and, or, unknownFutureValue.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"threshold_value":{"type":"string","description":"The threshold value of the alert condition. The threshold value can be a number in string form or string like 'WestUS'.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"list"},"description":"The conditions that determine when to send alerts.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"description":{"type":"string","description":"Optional description of the resource. Maximum length is 1500 characters.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"The display name of the rule.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"enabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether the rule is enabled.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier for the alert rule. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"is_system_rule":{"type":"bool","description":"Indicates whether the rule is a system rule. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"notification_channels":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"notification_channel_type":{"type":"string","description":"The type of the notification channel. Possible values: portal, email, phoneCall, sms, unknownFutureValue.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"notification_receivers":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"contact_information":{"type":"string","description":"Contact information for the receiver.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"locale":{"type":"string","description":"Locale for the receiver.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"list"},"description":"Notification receivers for the channel.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"list"},"description":"The notification channels of the rule.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"severity":{"type":"string","description":"The severity of the rule. Possible values: unknown, informational, warning, critical, unknownFutureValue.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"threshold":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"aggregation":{"type":"string","description":"Aggregation method. Possible values: count, percentage, affectedCloudPcCount, affectedCloudPcPercentage, unknownFutureValue.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"operator":{"type":"string","description":"Operator. Possible values: greaterOrEqual, equal, greater, less, lessOrEqual, notEqual, unknownFutureValue.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"target":{"type":"number","description":"The target threshold value.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"The conditions that determine when to send alerts. Deprecated. Use conditions instead.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"Manages a Windows 365 Cloud PC Alert Rule using the Microsoft Graph Beta API.","description_kind":"plain"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_windows_365_cloud_pc_device_image":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"The display name of this image.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"error_code":{"type":"string","description":"The error code of the status of the image that indicates why the upload failed, if applicable. Possible values are: internalServerError, sourceImageNotFound, osVersionNotSupported, sourceImageInvalid, sourceImageNotGeneralized, unknownFutureValue, vmAlreadyAzureAdJoined, paidSourceImageNotSupport, sourceImageNotSupportCustomizeVMName, sourceImageSizeExceedsLimitation, sourceImageWithDataDiskNotSupported, sourceImageWithDiskEncryptionSetNotSupported. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"expiration_date":{"type":"string","description":"The date when the image became unavailable. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier (ID) of the image resource on the Cloud PC. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"last_modified_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The data and time when the image was last modified. The timestamp represents date and time information using ISO 8601 format and is always in UTC. For example, midnight UTC on Jan 1, 2014 is 2014-01-01T00:00:00Z. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"operating_system":{"type":"string","description":"The operating system of the image. For example, Windows 10 Enterprise. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"os_build_number":{"type":"string","description":"The OS build version of the image. For example, 1909. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"os_status":{"type":"string","description":"The OS status of this image. Possible values are: supported, supportedWithWarning, unknown, unknownFutureValue. The default value is unknown. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"os_version_number":{"type":"string","description":"The operating system version of this image. For example, 10.0.22000.296. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"source_image_resource_id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the source image resource on Azure. The required ID format is: \"/subscriptions/{subscription-id}/resourceGroups/{resourceGroupName}/providers/Microsoft.Compute/images/{imageName}\".","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"status":{"type":"string","description":"The status of the image on the Cloud PC. Possible values are: pending, ready, warning, failed, unknownFutureValue. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"version":{"type":"string","description":"The image version. For example, 0.0.1 and 1.5.13.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"description":"Manages Windows 365 Cloud PC device images using the `/deviceManagement/virtualEndpoint/deviceImages` endpoint. This resource is used to upload and manage custom Windows images for Cloud PC provisioning.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_windows_365_cloud_pc_organization_settings":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"enable_mem_auto_enroll":{"type":"bool","description":"Specifies whether new Cloud PCs will be automatically enrolled in Microsoft Endpoint Manager (MEM). The default value is false.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"enable_single_sign_on":{"type":"bool","description":"True if the provisioned Cloud PC can be accessed by single sign-on. False indicates that the provisioned Cloud PC doesn't support this feature. Default value is false. Windows 365 users can use single sign-on to authenticate to Microsoft Entra ID with passwordless options (for example, FIDO keys) to access their Cloud PC. Optional.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The singleton ID for the Cloud PC organization settings.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"os_version":{"type":"string","description":"The version of the operating system (OS) to provision on Cloud PCs. Possible values: windows10, windows11, unknownFutureValue.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"user_account_type":{"type":"string","description":"The account type of the user on provisioned Cloud PCs. Possible values: standardUser, administrator, unknownFutureValue.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"windows_settings":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"language":{"type":"string","description":"The Windows language/region tag to use for language pack configuration and localization of the Cloud PC. The default value is en-US, which corresponds to English (United States).","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Represents the Cloud PC organization settings for a tenant. A tenant has only one cloudPcOrganizationSettings object. The default language value en-US.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true}},"description":"Manages the singleton Cloud PC organization settings for a tenant.","description_kind":"plain"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_windows_365_cloud_pc_provisioning_policy":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"alternate_resource_url":{"type":"string","description":"The URL of the alternate resource that links to this provisioning policy. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"apply_to_existing_cloud_pcs":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"microsoft_entra_single_sign_on_for_all_devices":{"type":"bool","description":"When true, Microsoft Entra single sign-on is applied to all existing Cloud PCs. Applied only during resource updates and not during resource creation. Default is false.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"region_or_azure_network_connection_for_all_devices":{"type":"bool","description":"When true, region or Azure network connection settings are applied to all existing Cloud PCs. Applied only during resource updates and not during resource creation. Default is false.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"region_or_azure_network_connection_for_select_devices":{"type":"bool","description":"When true, region or Azure network connection settings are applied only to selected Cloud PCs. Applied only during resource updates and not during resource creation. Default is false.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"If you change the network, image, region or single sign-on configuration in a provisioning policy,no change will occur for previously provisioned Cloud PCs. Newly provisioned or reprovisioned Cloud PCs will honor thechanges in your provisioning policy. To change the network or image of previously provisioned Cloud PCs to align with the changes,you must reprovision those Cloud PCs. To change the region or single sign-on of previously provisioned Cloud PCs to align with the changes,you must apply the changed configuration retrospectively using the apply_to_existing_cloud_pcs block.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"assignments":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"allotment_display_name":{"type":"string","description":"A display name for the allotment. Required when provisioning_type is 'shared', 'sharedByUser', or 'sharedByEntraGroup'.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allotment_license_count":{"type":"number","description":"The number of licenses to allot. Required when provisioning_type is 'shared', 'sharedByUser', or 'sharedByEntraGroup'.The number must be between 0 and 900 and can't be more than the number of shared Cloud PC licenses available.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"group_id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the Microsoft 365 group or security group in Microsoft Entra ID to assign the policy to.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"service_plan_id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the frontlineservice plan. Required when provisioning_type is 'shared', 'sharedByUser', or 'sharedByEntraGroup'.This value can be obtained from the 'microsoft365_graph_beta_windows_365_cloud_pc_frontline_service_plan' data source.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"type":{"type":"string","description":"The type of assignment target. Valid values are 'groupAssignmentTarget' only.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"Assignments of the Cloud PC provisioning policy to groups. Only Microsoft 365 groups and security groups in Microsoft Entra ID are currently supported.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"autopatch":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"autopatch_group_id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the autopatch group.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Autopatch settings for the provisioning policy.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"autopilot_configuration":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"application_timeout_in_minutes":{"type":"number","description":"The application timeout in minutes.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"device_preparation_profile_id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the device preparation profile.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"on_failure_device_access_denied":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether device access is denied on failure.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Autopilot configuration for the provisioning policy.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"cloud_pc_group_display_name":{"type":"string","description":"The display name of the Cloud PC group that the Cloud PCs reside in. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"cloud_pc_naming_template":{"type":"string","description":"Create unique names for your devices. Names must be between 5 and 15 characters, and can contain letters, numbers, and hyphens. Names cannot include a blank space. Use the %USERNAME:x% macro to add the first x letters of username. Use the %RAND:y% macro to add a random alphanumeric string of length y, y must be 5 or more. Names must contain a randomized string.For example, CPC-%USERNAME:4%-%RAND:5% means that the name of the Cloud PC starts with CPC-, followed by a four-character username, a - character, and then five random characters. The total length of the text generated by the template can't exceed 15 characters. Supports $filter, $select, and $orderby.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"description":{"type":"string","description":"Optional description of the resource. Maximum length is 1500 characters.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"The display name for the provisioning policy. May not contain any of the following characters: \u003c\u003e()\u0026|$'\",;^ and may not start or end with spaces.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"domain_join_configurations":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"domain_join_type":{"type":"string","description":"Specifies the method by which the provisioned Cloud PC joins Microsoft Entra ID.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"on_premises_connection_id":{"type":"string","description":"The Azure network connection ID that matches the virtual network IT admins want the provisioning policy to use when they create Cloud PCs.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"region_group":{"type":"string","description":"The Cloud PC region group. Must be one of: default, australia, canada, usCentral, usEast, usWest, france, germany, europeUnion, unitedKingdom, japan, asia, india, southAmerica, euap, usGovernment, usGovernmentDOD, unknownFutureValue, norway, switzerland, southKorea, middleEast, mexico, australasia, europe.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"region_name":{"type":"string","description":"The supported Azure region where the IT admin wants the provisioning policy to create Cloud PCs. It is recommended using the Automatic option.The option allows Windows 365 to make the best selection which decreases the chance of provisioning failure.Must be one of: automatic, japaneast, eastasia.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"list"},"description":"Specifies a list ordered by priority on how Cloud PCs join Microsoft Entra ID (Azure AD).","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"enable_single_sign_on":{"type":"bool","description":"True if the provisioned Cloud PC can be accessed by single sign-on. False indicates that the provisioned Cloud PC doesn't support this feature. The default value is false. ","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"grace_period_in_hours":{"type":"number","description":"The number of hours to wait before reprovisioning/deprovisioning happens. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier of the provisioning policy.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"image_display_name":{"type":"string","description":"The display name of the operating system image that is used for provisioning. Supports $filter, $select, and $orderBy.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"image_id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier that represents an operating system image used for provisioning new Cloud PCs. Must be one of:'microsoftwindowsdesktop_windows-ent-cpc_win11-25h2-ent-cpc','microsoftwindowsdesktop_windows-ent-cpc_win11-25h2-ent-cpc-m365','microsoftwindowsdesktop_windows-ent-cpc_win11-24H2-ent-cpc','microsoftwindowsdesktop_windows-ent-cpc_win11-24H2-ent-cpc-m365','microsoftwindowsdesktop_windows-ent-cpc_win11-23h2-ent-cpc-m365','microsoftwindowsdesktop_windows-ent-cpc_win11-23h2-ent-cpc'.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"image_type":{"type":"string","description":"The type of operating system image (custom or gallery) that is used for provisioning on Cloud PCs. Possible values are: gallery, custom. The default value is gallery. Supports $filter, $select, and $orderBy.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"managed_by":{"type":"string","description":"Specifies which service manages the Cloud PC provisioning policy. Possible values: windows365, devBox, unknownFutureValue, rpaBox. See Microsoft Graph documentation for details.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"microsoft_managed_desktop":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"managed_type":{"type":"string","description":"Indicates the provisioning policy associated with Microsoft Managed Desktop settings.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"profile":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the Microsoft Managed Desktop profile that the Windows 365 Cloud PC is associated with.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"This block is currently not supported in terraform. The registration to the Autopatch service currently only suports the intune gui,with no publically available api to call. This will return a 403 error if this block is used. Raise a ticket with Microsoft to make the Autopatch service available via api.The specific settings for Microsoft Managed Desktop that enables Microsoft Managed Desktop customers to get device managed experience for Cloud PC.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"provisioning_type":{"type":"string","description":"Specifies the type of license used when provisioning Cloud PCs using this policy.By default, the license type is dedicated if the provisioningType isn't specified when you create the cloudPcProvisioningPolicy.Possible values are: dedicated, shared, sharedByUser, sharedByEntraGroup, unknownFutureValue.Changes to this attribute will force recreation of the resource.dedicated: (Enterprise) Each user will get their own Cloud PC without restrictions on when they can connect to it.shared: (Frontline - Dedicated) Recommended for users who need part time access to their Cloud PCs or follow a set schedule, such as shifts. A single license lets you provision up to three Cloud PCs that can be used non-concurrently, each assigned to a single user. Provides one concurrent session.sharedByEntraGroup: (Frontline - Shared) Recommended for users who use Cloud PC for a short period of time and do not require data to be preserved. A single license lets you provision one Cloud PC that can be shared non-concurrently among a group of users. Provides one concurrent session.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"scope_ids":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"Set of scope tag IDs for this resource.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"windows_setting":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"locale":{"type":"string","description":"The Windows language or region tag to use for language pack configuration and localization of the Cloud PC. The default value is en-US, which corresponds to English (United States).","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Indicates a specific Windows setting to configure during the creation of Cloud PCs for this provisioning policy.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"description_kind":"plain"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_windows_365_cloud_pc_role_definition":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"description":{"type":"string","description":"Optional description of the resource. Maximum length is 1500 characters.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"Display Name of the Role definition.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"Key of the entity. This is read-only and automatically generated.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"is_built_in":{"type":"bool","description":"Type of Role. Set to True if it is built-in, or set to False if it is a custom role definition.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"is_built_in_role_definition":{"type":"bool","description":"Type of Role. Set to True if it is built-in, or set to False if it is a custom role definition.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"role_permissions":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"allowed_resource_actions":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"Allowed actions for this role permission. This field is equivalent to 'actions' and can be used interchangeably. The API will consolidate values from both fields. Each action must start with 'Microsoft.CloudPC/'.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"list"},"description":"List of Role Permissions this role is allowed to perform. Not used for in-built Cloud PC role definitions.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"Manages custom role definitions for Windows 365 using the `/roleManagement/cloudPC/roleDefinitions` endpoint. This resource is used to define sets of permissions that can be assigned to administrators for Cloud PC management, policy configuration, and administrative functions.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_windows_365_cloud_pc_user_setting":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"assignments":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"group_id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the Microsoft 365 group or security group in Microsoft Entra ID. Required when type is 'groupAssignmentTarget' or 'exclusionGroupAssignmentTarget'.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"type":{"type":"string","description":"The type of assignment target. Valid values are 'groupAssignmentTarget'.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"Assignments of the Cloud PC user setting to groups. Only Microsoft 365 groups and security groups in Microsoft Entra ID are currently supported.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"created_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time the setting was created. The timestamp type represents the date and time information using ISO 8601 format and is always in UTC. For example, midnight UTC on Jan 1, 2014 looks like this: '2014-01-01T00:00:00Z'.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"cross_region_disaster_recovery_setting":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"cross_region_disaster_recovery_enabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Indicates whether cross-region disaster recovery is enabled for the user's Cloud PC. When true, cross-region disaster recovery is enabled. The default value is false. This property is deprecated and will stop returning data on December 1, 2024.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"disaster_recovery_network_setting":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"network_type":{"type":"string","description":"The type of network for disaster recovery.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"region_group":{"type":"string","description":"The region group for the disaster recovery network. Default is 'usWest'.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"region_name":{"type":"string","description":"The region name for the disaster recovery network. Default is 'automatic'.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Indicates the network settings of the Cloud PC during a cross-region disaster recovery operation.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"disaster_recovery_type":{"type":"string","description":"Indicates the type of disaster recovery to perform when a disaster occurs on the user's Cloud PC.The possible values are: notConfigured, crossRegion, premium, unknownFutureValue. The default value is notConfigured.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"maintain_cross_region_restore_point_enabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Indicates whether Windows 365 maintain the cross-region disaster recovery function generated restore points.If true, the Windows 365 stored restore points; false indicates that Windows 365 doesn't generate or keep the restore point from the original Cloud PC. If a disaster occurs, the new Cloud PC can only be provisioned using the initial image.This limitation can result in the loss of some user data on the original Cloud PC. The default value is false.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"user_initiated_disaster_recovery_allowed":{"type":"bool","description":"Indicates whether the client allows the end user to initiate a disaster recovery activation.True indicates that the client includes the option for the end user to activate Backup Cloud PC. When false, the enduser doesn't have the option to activate disaster recovery. The default value is false. Currently, only premium disaster recovery is supported.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Defines whether the user's Cloud PC enables cross-region disaster recovery and specifies the network for the disaster recovery.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"The setting name displayed in the user interface.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"Unique identifier for the Cloud PC user setting. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"last_modified_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The last date and time the setting was modified. The timestamp type represents the date and time information using ISO 8601 format and is always in UTC. For example, midnight UTC on Jan 1, 2014 looks like this: '2014-01-01T00:00:00Z'.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"local_admin_enabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Indicates whether the local admin option is enabled. Default value is false. To enable the local admin option, change the setting to true. If the local admin option is enabled, the end user can be an admin of the Cloud PC device.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"notification_setting":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"restart_prompts_disabled":{"type":"bool","description":"If true, doesn't prompt the user to restart the Cloud PC. If false, prompts the user to restart Cloud PC. The default value is false.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Defines the setting of the Cloud PC notification prompts for the Cloud PC user.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"reset_enabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Indicates whether an end user is allowed to reset their Cloud PC. When true, the user is allowed to reset their Cloud PC. When false, end-user initiated reset isn't allowed. The default value is false.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"restore_point_setting":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"frequency_in_hours":{"type":"number","description":"The frequency in hours at which restore points are created.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"frequency_type":{"type":"string","description":"The time interval in hours to take snapshots (restore points) of a Cloud PC automatically. Possible values are: default, fourHours, sixHours, twelveHours, sixteenHours, twentyFourHours, unknownFutureValue. The default value is default that indicates that the time interval for automatic capturing of restore point snapshots is set to 12 hours.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"user_restore_enabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Indicates whether the user is allowed to restore their own Cloud PCs.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Defines how frequently a restore point is created that is, a snapshot is taken) for users' provisioned Cloud PCs (default is 12 hours), and whether the user is allowed to restore their own Cloud PCs to a backup made at a specific point in time.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"self_service_enabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Indicates whether the self-service option is enabled. Default value is false. To enable the self-service option, change the setting to true. If the self-service option is enabled, the end user is allowed to perform some self-service operations, such as upgrading the Cloud PC through the end user portal. The **selfServiceEnabled** property is deprecated and will stop returning data on December 1, 2023.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description_kind":"plain"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_windows_updates_autopatch_content_approval":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"catalog_entry_id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the catalog entry to approve for deployment. This should reference a feature or quality update from the Windows Update catalog.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"catalog_entry_type":{"type":"string","description":"The type of catalog entry being approved. Valid values are: `featureUpdate`, `qualityUpdate`.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"created_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time when the content approval was created.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"deployment_settings":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"schedule":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"gradual_rollout":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"end_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time when the gradual rollout should complete.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Settings for gradual rollout of the deployment.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"start_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time when the deployment should start.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Schedule settings for the deployment.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Settings for governing how to deploy the approved content.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"Unique identifier for the content approval (compliance change ID).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"is_revoked":{"type":"bool","description":"Set to `true` to revoke the content approval, preventing further deployment. Revoking is a final action and cannot be undone.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"revoked_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time when the content approval was revoked.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update_policy_id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the Windows Update policy to which this content approval belongs.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"description":"Manages Windows Update content approvals using the `/admin/windows/updates/updatePolicies/{updatePolicyId}/complianceChanges` endpoint. Content approvals define which updates (feature or quality) should be deployed to devices according to a specific update policy. This resource requires an existing update policy and references catalog entries from the Windows Update catalog.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_windows_updates_autopatch_deployment":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"content":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"catalog_entry_id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the catalog entry to deploy. This should reference a feature or quality update from the Windows Update catalog. Cannot be changed after creation and will require a replacement to update.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"catalog_entry_type":{"type":"string","description":"The type of catalog entry being deployed. Valid values are: `featureUpdate`, `qualityUpdate`.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Specifies what content to deploy. Cannot be changed after creation.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"created_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time when the deployment was created.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"Unique identifier for the deployment.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"last_modified_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time when the deployment was last modified.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"settings":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"content_applicability":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"safeguard":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"disabled_safeguard_profiles":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"category":{"type":"string","description":"The category of safeguard to disable. Valid values are: `likelyIssues`.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"List of safeguard profiles to disable for this deployment. By default, all safeguards are applied.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Safeguard settings to control which safeguard holds are applied to the deployment.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Content applicability settings for the deployment, including safeguard configurations.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"expedite":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"is_expedited":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether this deployment should be expedited. When `true`, the update overrides device policies and installs as quickly as possible.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"is_readiness_test":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether this is a readiness test for expedited updates. Used to verify devices meet prerequisites before actual expedited deployment.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Expedite settings for quality updates. Used to bypass Windows Update for Business deferral policies and deploy updates as quickly as possible.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"monitoring":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"monitoring_rules":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"action":{"type":"string","description":"The action to take when the monitoring threshold is met. Valid values are: `alertError`, `offerFallback`, `pauseDeployment`.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"signal":{"type":"string","description":"The signal to monitor. Valid values are: `rollback` or `ineligible`.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"threshold":{"type":"number","description":"The percentage of devices that trigger the action. Required for `rollback` signal. Must not be set when `action` is `offerFallback` (the fallback is offered to all ineligible devices unconditionally).","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"Rules for monitoring the deployment and the action that should be taken when the signal threshold is met.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Monitoring settings for the deployment.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"schedule":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"gradual_rollout":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"devices_per_offer":{"type":"number","description":"The number of devices to offer the update to in each rollout wave.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"duration_between_offers":{"type":"string","description":"The duration between each offer in ISO 8601 format (e.g., `P7D` for 7 days).","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"end_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time when the gradual rollout should complete. Must be in ISO 8601 format.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Settings for gradual rollout of the deployment.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"start_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time when the deployment should start. Must be in ISO 8601 format.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Schedule settings for the deployment.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"user_experience":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"days_until_forced_reboot":{"type":"number","description":"Number of days after installation before the device is forced to reboot. Valid for expedited quality updates. If not specified, uses device policy defaults.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"offer_as_optional":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether to offer the update as optional to end users. When `true`, users can choose when to install. When `false` (default), the update is offered as recommended.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"User experience settings for the deployment. These settings control how the update is presented to end users.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Settings specified on the deployment governing how to deploy content. Settings may be added to a deployment that was created without them, but once configured they cannot be modified in place — changes will require the resource to be replaced.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"Manages Windows Update deployments for deploying content to a set of devices using the `/admin/windows/updates/deployments` endpoint. Deployments define which update content (feature or quality updates) should be deployed, to which audience, and with what settings (schedule, monitoring, etc.). ","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_windows_updates_autopatch_deployment_audience":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"exclusions":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"Set of device or Entra group IDs to exclude from the deployment audience.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier for the deployment audience.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"member_type":{"type":"string","description":"The type of members in this audience. All members and exclusions must be of the same type. Valid values are: `azureADDevice`, `updatableAssetGroup`. Defaults to `azureADDevice`.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"members":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"Set of device or Entra group IDs to include in the deployment audience.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"Manages a Windows Update deployment audience in Microsoft 365, including its members and exclusions. Uses the `/admin/windows/updates/deploymentAudiences` endpoint to create the audience container and the `updateAudienceById` action to manage members and exclusions in a single resource. See the [Microsoft Graph API documentation](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/graph/api/resources/windowsupdates-deploymentaudience?view=graph-rest-beta) for more information.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_windows_updates_autopatch_deployment_state":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"deployment_id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the deployment whose state is being managed.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"effective_value":{"type":"string","description":"The effective state value of the deployment. Possible values: `scheduled`, `offering`, `paused`, `faulted`, `archived` (read-only).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the deployment (same as deployment_id).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"requested_value":{"type":"string","description":"The requested state of the deployment. Valid values are: `none` (active/offering), `paused`, `archived`.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"Manages the lifecycle state of a Windows Update autopatch deployment. Using the `/admin/windows/updates/deployments/{deploymentId}/update` endpoint. This resource allows pausing, resuming, or archiving a deployment independently from its configuration. The deployment must be created first using the `microsoft365_graph_beta_windows_updates_autopatch_deployment` resource. ","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_windows_updates_autopatch_device_registration":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"entra_device_object_ids":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"Set of Entra ID device object IDs to enroll in Windows Autopatch for the specified update category. These are the 'id' property from the Entra ID device object, NOT the 'deviceId' property.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The composite identifier for this resource. Format: `{update_category}`.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update_category":{"type":"string","description":"The category of updates for Windows Autopatch to manage. Valid values are: `driver`, `feature`, `quality`.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"description":"Manages batch enrollment of Entra ID devices in Windows Autopatch update management using the `/admin/windows/updates/updatableAssets/enrollAssetsById` endpoint. This resource enrolls multiple devices for a specific update category (driver, feature, or quality updates). Devices are automatically created as azureADDevice resources in Windows Autopatch if they don't already exist. When the resource is deleted, devices are unenrolled from the specified update category. ","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_windows_updates_autopatch_operational_insights_connection":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"azure_resource_group_name":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the Azure resource group that contains the Log Analytics workspace.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"azure_subscription_id":{"type":"string","description":"The Azure subscription ID that contains the Log Analytics workspace.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier for the Operational Insights connection.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"state":{"type":"string","description":"The state of the connection. Possible values: `connected`, `notAuthorized`, `notFound`, `unknownFutureValue` (read-only).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"workspace_name":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the Log Analytics workspace.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"description":"Manages a Windows Update Operational Insights connection using the `/admin/windows/updates/resourceConnections` endpoint. An Operational Insights connection links Windows Update for Business deployment service to an Azure Log Analytics workspace, enabling deployment reporting and insights. This resource does not support in-place updates — any change to a field will destroy and recreate the connection.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_windows_updates_autopatch_policy":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"approval_rules":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"cadence":{"type":"string","description":"The cadence of the quality update. Possible values are: `monthly`, `outOfBand`.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"classification":{"type":"string","description":"The classification of the quality update. Possible values are: `all`, `security`, `nonSecurity`.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"deferral_in_days":{"type":"number","description":"The Windows update deferral period in days. The value must be between 0 and 30.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"The approval rules that determine which published content matches the rule on an ongoing basis.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"created_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time when the policy was created. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"description":{"type":"string","description":"The policy description. The maximum length is 1,500 characters.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"The policy display name. The maximum length is 200 characters.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier for the Windows Autopatch policy.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"last_modified_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time when the policy was last modified. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"Manages a Windows Autopatch quality update policy using the `/admin/windows/updates/policies` endpoint. A quality update policy defines approval rules that determine which published Windows quality updates are automatically approved for deployment based on classification (security/nonSecurity) and cadence (monthly/outOfBand).","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_windows_updates_autopatch_policy_approval":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"catalog_entry_id":{"type":"string","description":"The catalog entry ID to approve. References a quality update from the Windows Update catalog. This field cannot be changed after creation — changes require the resource to be replaced.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"created_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time the policy approval was created (read-only).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier for the policy approval.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"last_modified_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time the policy approval was last modified (read-only).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"policy_id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the Windows Update policy to which this approval belongs.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"status":{"type":"string","description":"The approval status. Valid values are: `approved`, `suspended`.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"Manages a Windows Update policy approval using the `/admin/windows/updates/policies/{policyId}/approvals` endpoint. A policy approval grants or suspends approval for a specific catalog entry (quality update) within a Windows Update policy. The policy must already exist, managed by the `microsoft365_graph_beta_windows_updates_autopatch_policy` resource.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_windows_updates_autopatch_ring":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"created_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time the ring was created (read-only).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"deferral_in_days":{"type":"number","description":"The quality update deferral period in days. The value must be between 0 and 30.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"description":{"type":"string","description":"The ring description. The maximum length is 1,500 characters.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"The ring display name. The maximum length is 200 characters.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"excluded_group_assignment":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"assignments":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"group_id":{"type":"string","description":"The Microsoft Entra group ID to exclude from this ring.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"A set of group assignments governing the excluded deployment audience.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Defines the Microsoft Entra groups whose devices are excluded from this ring's deployment audience. If not set, an empty assignment is sent.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier for the ring.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"included_group_assignment":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"assignments":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"group_id":{"type":"string","description":"The Microsoft Entra group ID to include in this ring.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"A set of group assignments governing the included deployment audience.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Defines the Microsoft Entra groups whose devices are included in this ring's deployment audience. If not set, an empty assignment is sent.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"is_hotpatch_enabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether hotpatch updates are enabled for this ring (quality update rings only). Hotpatch updates apply without requiring a device restart.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"is_paused":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether the ring is paused. When `true`, quality update deployment to devices in this ring is halted.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"last_modified_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time the ring was last modified (read-only).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"policy_id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the Windows Update policy to which this ring belongs.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"Manages a Windows Update policy ring using the `/admin/windows/updates/policies/{policyId}/rings` endpoint. A ring defines the deployment audience, deferral, and pause settings for quality updates within a Windows Update policy. The policy must already exist, managed by the `microsoft365_graph_beta_windows_updates_autopatch_policy` resource.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_windows_updates_autopatch_updatable_asset_group":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"entra_device_object_ids":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"Set of Entra ID device object IDs to add as members of the updatable asset group. Omit or leave empty to create a group with no initial members.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier for the updatable asset group.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"Manages a Windows Autopatch updatable asset group and its Entra ID device membership using the `/admin/windows/updates/updatableAssets` endpoint. Creating the resource provisions an empty group container. The optional `entra_device_object_ids` attribute manages which Entra ID devices (by object ID) are members of the group. Membership changes are diff-based: on update only the delta is applied via `addMembersById` and `removeMembersById`. Deleting the resource permanently removes the group and all its memberships.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_windows_updates_update_policy":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"audience_id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the deployment audience to target with this policy.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"compliance_change_rules":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"content_filter":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"filter_type":{"type":"string","description":"The type of content filter. Only `driverUpdateFilter` is supported. Note: `windowsUpdateFilter` is not valid despite appearing in API documentation.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"The content filter for the compliance change rule.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"created_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time when the rule was created. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"duration_before_deployment_start":{"type":"string","description":"The duration before deployment starts (ISO 8601 duration format). Valid range: P1D to P30D (1 to 30 days). Cannot be updated after creation. Examples: 'P7D' for 7 days, 'P14D' for 14 days.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"last_evaluated_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time when the rule was last evaluated. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"last_modified_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time when the rule was last modified. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"Rules for governing the automatic creation of compliance changes. Cannot be updated after creation - changes require resource replacement.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"compliance_changes":{"type":"bool","description":"Enable compliance changes (content approvals) for this policy. Must be set to `true` to create content approvals.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"created_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time when the update policy was created. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"deployment_settings":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"schedule":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"gradual_rollout":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"devices_per_offer":{"type":"number","description":"The number of devices to offer the update to in each batch. Must be a positive integer (minimum 1).","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"duration_between_offers":{"type":"string","description":"The duration between offers (ISO 8601 duration format). Valid range: P1D to P30D (1 to 30 days). Examples: 'P1D' for 1 day, 'P7D' for 7 days.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Settings for gradual rollout.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"start_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The start date and time for the deployment (ISO 8601 format).","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Settings for the schedule of the deployment.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Settings for governing how to deploy content.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier for the update policy.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"Manages a Windows Update policy using the `/admin/windows/updates/updatePolicies` endpoint. An update policy serves as a container for compliance changes (content approvals) that define which updates should be deployed to devices. This resource is a prerequisite for creating content approvals.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_device_management_device_configuration_assignment":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"device_configuration_id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the device configuration policy to assign.","description_kind":"plain","required":true},"group_id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the Azure AD group to assign the device configuration to.\n\n**Required when:**\n- `target_type` is `groupAssignment` or `exclusionGroupAssignment`\n- `target_type` is `configurationManagerCollection` (represents the collection ID)\n\n**Not used when:**\n- `target_type` is `allDevices` or `allLicensedUsers`","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier of the device configuration assignment.","description_kind":"plain","computed":true},"target_type":{"type":"string","description":"The target group type for the device configuration assignment. Possible values are:\n\n- **allDevices**: Target all devices in the tenant\n- **allLicensedUsers**: Target all licensed users in the tenant\n- **configurationManagerCollection**: Target System Centre Configuration Manager collection\n- **exclusionGroupAssignment**: Target a specific Entra ID group for exclusion\n- **groupAssignment**: Target a specific Entra ID group","description_kind":"plain","required":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"Manages device configuration assignments using the `/deviceManagement/deviceConfigurations/{deviceConfigurationId}/assignments` endpoint. This resource is used to controls assignments for device configurations.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_identity_and_access_conditional_access_terms_of_use":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"Display name of the agreement. The display name is used for internal tracking of the agreement but isn't shown to end users who view the agreement.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"file":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"localizations":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"Localized display name of the policy file of an agreement. The localized display name is shown to end users who view the agreement.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"file_data":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"data":{"type":"string","description":"Data that represents the terms of use PDF document as raw bytes (base64 encoded).","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Data that represents the terms of use PDF document. Must be provided during creation but is not returned by the API and will always be null in state. This field is intentionally not persisted for security reasons.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"file_name":{"type":"string","description":"Name of the agreement file (for example, TOU.pdf).","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"is_default":{"type":"bool","description":"If none of the languages matches the client preference, indicates whether this is the default agreement file. If none of the files are marked as default, the first one is treated as the default. Must be true if the language is 'en-US'.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"is_major_version":{"type":"bool","description":"Indicates whether the agreement file is a major version update. Major version updates invalidate the agreement's acceptances on the corresponding language.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"language":{"type":"string","description":"The language of the agreement file. When `is_default` is `true`, must be `en-US` (full format with country code). When `is_default` is `false`, must use only the two-letter language code (e.g., `en`, `fr`, `de`). The language code is a lowercase two-letter code derived from ISO 639-1.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"The localized version of the terms of use agreement files attached to the agreement.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Default PDF linked to this agreement. This is required when creating a new agreement.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier for the agreement. This is automatically generated when the agreement is created.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"is_per_device_acceptance_required":{"type":"bool","description":"This setting enables you to require end users to accept this agreement on every device that they're accessing it from. The end user is required to register their device in Microsoft Entra ID, if they haven't already done so.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"is_viewing_before_acceptance_required":{"type":"bool","description":"Indicates whether the user has to expand the agreement before accepting.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"terms_expiration":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"frequency":{"type":"string","description":"Represents the frequency at which the terms will expire, after its first expiration as set in startDateTime. Must be in ISO 8601 duration format.\n\n**Accepted values:**\n- `P365D` - Annually (365 days)\n- `P180D` - Bi-annually (180 days)\n- `P90D` - Quarterly (90 days)\n- `P30D` - Monthly (30 days)","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"start_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date when the agreement is set to expire for all users. Must be in YYYY-MM-DD format (e.g., `2025-12-31`) and is always in UTC time. The time portion (T00:00:00Z) will be automatically appended.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Expiration schedule and frequency of agreement for all users.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"user_reaccept_required_frequency":{"type":"string","description":"The duration after which the user must reaccept the terms of use. Must be in ISO 8601 duration format (e.g., `P90D`).\n\n**Common values:**\n- `P365D` - Annually (365 days)\n- `P180D` - Bi-annually (180 days)\n- `P90D` - Quarterly (90 days)\n- `P30D` - Monthly (30 days)\n- `P270D` - 270 days","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true}},"description":"Manages Microsoft 365 Terms of Use Agreements using the `/agreements` endpoint. This resource is used to terms of use agreements allow organizations to present information that users must accept before accessing data or applications. These agreements can be used to ensure compliance with legal or regulatory requirements..","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_m365_admin_m365_apps_installation_options":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"apps_for_mac":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"is_microsoft_365_apps_enabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Specifies whether users can install Microsoft 365 apps on their MAC devices. The default value is `true`.","description_kind":"plain","required":true},"is_skype_for_business_enabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Specifies whether users can install Skype for Business on their MAC devices running OS X El Capitan 10.11 or later. The default value is `true`.","description_kind":"plain","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"The Microsoft 365 apps installation options container object for a MAC platform.","description_kind":"plain","required":true},"apps_for_windows":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"is_microsoft_365_apps_enabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Specifies whether users can install Microsoft 365 apps, including Skype for Business, on their Windows devices. The default value is `true`.","description_kind":"plain","required":true},"is_skype_for_business_enabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Specifies whether users can install Skype for Business (standalone) on their Windows devices. The default value is `true`.","description_kind":"plain","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"The Microsoft 365 apps installation options container object for a Windows platform.","description_kind":"plain","required":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier of the M365 Apps Installation Options.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update_channel":{"type":"string","description":"Specifies how often users get feature updates for Microsoft 365 apps installed on devices running Windows. The possible values are: `current`, `monthlyEnterprise`, or `semiAnnual`, with corresponding update frequencies of `As soon as they're ready`, `Once a month`, and `Every six months`.","description_kind":"plain","required":true}},"description":"Manages Microsoft 365 Apps installation options using the `/admin/microsoft365Apps/installationOptions` endpoint. This resource is used to installation options control tenant-wide settings for M365 Apps deployment including update channels, app availability for Windows and macOS platforms, and feature restrictions for organizational software distribution governance.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_powershell_microsoft_teams_teams_calling_policy":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"ai_interpreter":{"type":"string","description":"Enables the user to use the AI Interpreter related features.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_call_forwarding_to_phone":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow call forwarding to phone.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_call_forwarding_to_user":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow call forwarding to user.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_call_groups":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow call groups.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_call_redirect":{"type":"string","description":"Allow call redirect. Valid values: Enabled, Disabled.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_cloud_recording_for_calls":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow cloud recording for calls.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_delegation":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow delegation.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_private_calling":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow private calling.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_sip_devices_calling":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow SIP devices calling.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_transcription_for_calling":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow transcription for calling.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_voicemail":{"type":"string","description":"Allow voicemail. Valid values: AlwaysEnabled, AlwaysDisabled, UserOverride.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_web_pstn_calling":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow web PSTN calling.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"auto_answer_enabled_type":{"type":"string","description":"Auto answer enabled type.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"busy_on_busy_enabled_type":{"type":"string","description":"Busy on busy enabled type.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"call_recording_expiration_days":{"type":"number","description":"Call recording expiration days.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"calling_spend_user_limit":{"type":"number","description":"Calling spend user limit.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"copilot":{"type":"string","description":"Copilot setting.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"description":{"type":"string","description":"Optional description of the resource. Maximum length is 1500 characters.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"enable_spend_limits":{"type":"bool","description":"Enable spend limits.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"enable_web_pstn_media_bypass":{"type":"bool","description":"Enable web PSTN media bypass.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The name (Identity) of the Teams Calling Policy.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"inbound_federated_call_routing_treatment":{"type":"string","description":"Inbound federated call routing treatment.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"inbound_pstn_call_routing_treatment":{"type":"string","description":"Inbound PSTN call routing treatment.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"live_captions_enabled_type_for_calling":{"type":"string","description":"Live captions enabled type for calling.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"music_on_hold_enabled_type":{"type":"string","description":"Music on hold enabled type.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"popout_app_path_for_incoming_pstn_calls":{"type":"string","description":"Popout app path for incoming PSTN calls.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"popout_for_incoming_pstn_calls":{"type":"string","description":"Popout for incoming PSTN calls.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"prevent_toll_bypass":{"type":"bool","description":"Prevent toll bypass.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"real_time_text":{"type":"string","description":"Real time text.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"spam_filtering_enabled_type":{"type":"string","description":"Spam filtering enabled type.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"voice_simulation_in_interpreter":{"type":"string","description":"Voice simulation in interpreter.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true}},"description":"Manages a Microsoft Teams Calling Policy using PowerShell cmdlets. See [Set-CsTeamsCallingPolicy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/powershell/module/teams/set-csteamscallingpolicy?view=teams-ps) and [New-CsTeamsCallingPolicy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/powershell/module/teams/new-csteamscallingpolicy?view=teams-ps).","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_powershell_microsoft_teams_teams_meeting_policy":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"ai_interpreter":{"type":"string","description":"Enables the user to use the AI Interpreter related features.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_annotations":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow users to use the Annotation feature.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_anonymous_users_to_dial_out":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow anonymous users to dial out to a PSTN number.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_anonymous_users_to_join_meeting":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow anonymous users to join meetings.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_anonymous_users_to_start_meeting":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow anonymous users to start meetings.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_avatars_in_gallery":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow avatars in gallery view.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_breakout_rooms":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow breakout rooms in meetings.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_carbon_summary":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow carbon summary in meetings.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_cart_captions_scheduling":{"type":"string","description":"Allow scheduling of CART captions.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_channel_meeting_scheduling":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow scheduling of channel meetings.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_cloud_recording":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow cloud recording in meetings.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_document_collaboration":{"type":"string","description":"Allow document collaboration in meetings.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_engagement_report":{"type":"string","description":"Allow engagement report in meetings.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_external_non_trusted_meeting_chat":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow chat for external non-trusted users in meetings.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_external_participant_give_request_control":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow external participants to give/request control.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_immersive_view":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow immersive view in meetings.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_ip_audio":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow IP audio in meetings.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_ip_video":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow IP video in meetings.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_local_recording":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow local recording in meetings.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_meet_now":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow Meet Now in meetings.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_meeting_coach":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow meeting coach in meetings.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_meeting_reactions":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow meeting reactions in meetings.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_meeting_registration":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow meeting registration.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_ndi_streaming":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow NDI streaming in meetings.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_network_configuration_settings_lookup":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow network configuration settings lookup.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_organizers_to_override_lobby_settings":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow organizers to override lobby settings.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_outlook_add_in":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow Outlook add-in for meetings.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_participant_give_request_control":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow participants to give/request control.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_power_point_sharing":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow PowerPoint sharing in meetings.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_private_meet_now":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow private Meet Now in meetings.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_private_meeting_scheduling":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow private meeting scheduling.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_pstn_users_to_bypass_lobby":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow PSTN users to bypass lobby.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_recording_storage_outside_region":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow recording storage outside region.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_screen_content_digitization":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow screen content digitization.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_shared_notes":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow shared notes in meetings.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_tasks_from_transcript":{"type":"string","description":"Allow tasks from transcript.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_tracking_in_report":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow tracking in report.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_transcription":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow transcription in meetings.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_user_to_join_external_meeting":{"type":"string","description":"Allow user to join external meeting.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_watermark_customization_for_camera_video":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow watermark customization for camera video.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_watermark_customization_for_screen_sharing":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow watermark customization for screen sharing.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_watermark_for_camera_video":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow watermark for camera video.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_watermark_for_screen_sharing":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow watermark for screen sharing.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allow_whiteboard":{"type":"bool","description":"Allow whiteboard in meetings.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allowed_streaming_media_input":{"type":"string","description":"Allowed streaming media input.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allowed_users_for_meeting_context":{"type":"string","description":"Allowed users for meeting context.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"allowed_users_for_meeting_details":{"type":"string","description":"Allowed users for meeting details.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"anonymous_user_authentication_method":{"type":"string","description":"Anonymous user authentication method.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"attendee_identity_masking":{"type":"string","description":"Attendee identity masking.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"audible_recording_notification":{"type":"string","description":"Audible recording notification.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"auto_admitted_users":{"type":"string","description":"Auto admitted users.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"auto_recording":{"type":"string","description":"Auto recording setting.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"automatically_start_copilot":{"type":"string","description":"Automatically start Copilot.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"blocked_anonymous_join_client_types":{"type":["list","string"],"description":"Blocked anonymous join client types.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"captcha_verification_for_meeting_join":{"type":"string","description":"Captcha verification for meeting join.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"channel_recording_download":{"type":"string","description":"Channel recording download setting.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"connect_to_meeting_controls":{"type":"string","description":"Connect to meeting controls.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"content_sharing_in_external_meetings":{"type":"string","description":"Content sharing in external meetings.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"copilot":{"type":"string","description":"Copilot setting.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"copy_restriction":{"type":"bool","description":"Copy restriction setting.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"description":{"type":"string","description":"Optional description of the resource. Maximum length is 1500 characters.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"designated_presenter_role_mode":{"type":"string","description":"Designated presenter role mode.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"detect_sensitive_content_during_screen_sharing":{"type":"bool","description":"Detect sensitive content during screen sharing.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"enroll_user_override":{"type":"string","description":"Enroll user override setting.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"explicit_recording_consent":{"type":"string","description":"Explicit recording consent setting.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"external_meeting_join":{"type":"string","description":"External meeting join setting.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The name (Identity) of the Teams Meeting Policy.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"info_shown_in_report_mode":{"type":"string","description":"Info shown in report mode.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"ip_audio_mode":{"type":"string","description":"IP audio mode.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"ip_video_mode":{"type":"string","description":"IP video mode.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"live_captions_enabled_type":{"type":"string","description":"Live captions enabled type.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"live_interpretation_enabled_type":{"type":"string","description":"Live interpretation enabled type.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"live_streaming_mode":{"type":"string","description":"Live streaming mode.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"lobby_chat":{"type":"string","description":"Lobby chat setting.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"media_bit_rate_kb":{"type":"number","description":"Maximum media bit rate in Kb.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"meeting_chat_enabled_type":{"type":"string","description":"Meeting chat enabled type.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"meeting_invite_languages":{"type":"string","description":"Meeting invite languages.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"new_meeting_recording_expiration_days":{"type":"number","description":"Number of days before new meeting recordings expire.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"noise_suppression_for_dial_in_participants":{"type":"string","description":"Noise suppression for dial-in participants.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"participant_name_change":{"type":"string","description":"Participant name change setting.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"participant_slide_control":{"type":"string","description":"Participant slide control setting.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"preferred_meeting_provider_for_islands_mode":{"type":"string","description":"Preferred meeting provider for Islands mode.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"qna_engagement_mode":{"type":"string","description":"QnA engagement mode.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"real_time_text":{"type":"string","description":"Real time text setting.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"recording_storage_mode":{"type":"string","description":"Recording storage mode.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"room_attribute_user_override":{"type":"string","description":"Room attribute user override.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"room_people_name_user_override":{"type":"string","description":"Room people name user override.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"screen_sharing_mode":{"type":"string","description":"Screen sharing mode.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"sms_notifications":{"type":"string","description":"SMS notifications setting.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"speaker_attribution_mode":{"type":"string","description":"Speaker attribution mode.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"streaming_attendee_mode":{"type":"string","description":"Streaming attendee mode.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"teams_camera_far_end_ptz_mode":{"type":"string","description":"Teams camera far end PTZ mode.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"tenant":{"type":"string","description":"Tenant GUID.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"users_can_admit_from_lobby":{"type":"string","description":"Users who can admit from lobby.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"video_filters_mode":{"type":"string","description":"Video filters mode.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"voice_isolation":{"type":"string","description":"Voice isolation setting.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"voice_simulation_in_interpreter":{"type":"string","description":"Voice simulation in interpreter setting.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"watermark_for_anonymous_users":{"type":"string","description":"Watermark for anonymous users.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"watermark_for_camera_video_opacity":{"type":"number","description":"Watermark opacity for camera video.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"watermark_for_camera_video_pattern":{"type":"string","description":"Watermark pattern for camera video.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"watermark_for_screen_sharing_opacity":{"type":"number","description":"Watermark opacity for screen sharing.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"watermark_for_screen_sharing_pattern":{"type":"string","description":"Watermark pattern for screen sharing.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"who_can_register":{"type":"string","description":"Who can register for meetings.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"xds_identity":{"type":"string","description":"The XDS identity of the Teams Meeting Policy.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"description":"Manages a Microsoft Teams Meeting Policy using PowerShell cmdlets. The CsTeamsMeetingPolicy cmdlets enable administrators to control the type of meetings that users can create or the features that they can access while in a meeting. It also helps determine how meetings deal with anonymous or external users.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_utility_guid_list_sharder":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"group_id":{"type":"string","description":"The object ID of the group to query members from. Required when `resource_type = \"group_members\"`, ignored otherwise. Use this to split an existing group's membership into multiple new groups for targeted policy application.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of this resource.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"odata_filter":{"type":"string","description":"Optional OData filter expression applied at the API level before sharding. **Users:** `accountEnabled eq true` (active accounts only), `userType eq 'Member'` (exclude guests). **Devices:** `operatingSystem eq 'Windows'` (Windows devices only). **Service Principals:** `startswith(displayName, 'Microsoft')` (Microsoft apps), `appId eq 'guid'` (specific app). Leave empty to query all resources without filtering.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"recalculate_on_next_run":{"type":"bool","description":"Controls whether shard assignments are recomputed during Terraform plan/refresh and on `terraform apply` when configuration changes.\n\n**`false` (recommended default):** Shard assignments are locked in state. No Graph API call is made during plan or apply, and membership changes in your tenant (users added, removed) do not cause reassignments. On the very first apply, when no prior state exists, assignments are always computed regardless of this value — so you can safely set `false` from the outset without a two-step toggle.\n\n**`true`:** Re-queries the Graph API and reruns the sharding algorithm on every plan refresh and every apply. Use this only when you explicitly want to rebalance — for example after a large onboarding wave, a policy restructure, or a change to `shard_count` or `strategy`.\n\n**Recommended workflow:** Set to `false` from day one. Initial assignments are computed automatically on the first apply. Change to `true` (and run `terraform apply`) only when you intentionally want to reshard. Set back to `false` afterwards to re-lock assignments.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"resource_type":{"type":"string","description":"The type of Microsoft Graph resource to query and shard. `users` queries `/users` for user-based policies (MFA, conditional access). `devices` queries `/devices` for device policies (Windows Updates, compliance). `applications` queries `/applications` for app registrations. `service_principals` queries `/servicePrincipals` (enterprise apps) for application-based conditional access policies. `group_members` queries `/groups/{id}/members` to split existing group membership (requires `group_id`).","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"seed":{"type":"string","description":"Optional seed value for deterministic distribution. When provided, makes results reproducible across Terraform runs for the same input set. **`round-robin`**: No seed = uses API order (may change). With seed = shuffles deterministically first, then round-robin. **`percentage`/`size`**: Same shuffle behaviour as round-robin. **`rendezvous`**: Always deterministic. Seed affects which shard each GUID is assigned to. Use different seeds for different rollouts to vary pilot burden distribution.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"shard_count":{"type":"number","description":"Number of equally-sized shards to create (minimum 1). Use with `round-robin` strategy. Conflicts with `shard_percentages` and `shard_sizes`. Creates shards named `shard_0`, `shard_1`, ..., `shard_N-1`.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"shard_percentages":{"type":["list","number"],"description":"List of percentages for custom-sized shards. Use with `percentage` strategy. Conflicts with `shard_count` and `shard_sizes`. Values must be non-negative integers that sum to exactly 100. Example: `[10, 30, 60]` creates 10% pilot, 30% broader pilot, 60% full rollout.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"shard_sizes":{"type":["list","number"],"description":"List of absolute shard sizes (exact number of GUIDs per shard). Use with `size` strategy. Conflicts with `shard_count` and `shard_percentages`. Values must be positive integers or -1 (which means 'all remaining'). Only the last element can be -1. Example: `[50, 200, -1]` creates 50 pilot users, 200 broader rollout, remainder for full deployment.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"shards":{"type":["map",["set","string"]],"description":"Computed map of shard names (`shard_0`, `shard_1`, ...) to sets of GUIDs. Each value is a `set(string)` type, directly compatible with resource attributes expecting object ID sets. Access with `resource.example.shards[\"shard_0\"]`, check size with `length(resource.example.shards[\"shard_0\"])`.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"strategy":{"type":"string","description":"The distribution strategy for sharding GUIDs. `round-robin` distributes in circular order (guarantees equal sizes, optional seed for reproducibility). `percentage` distributes by specified percentages (requires `shard_percentages`, optional seed for reproducibility). `size` distributes by absolute sizes (requires `shard_sizes`, optional seed for reproducibility). `rendezvous` uses Highest Random Weight algorithm (always deterministic, minimal disruption when shard count changes).","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"Retrieves object IDs (GUIDs) from Microsoft Graph API and distributes them into configurable shards for progressive rollouts and phased deployments. Queries `/users`, `/devices`, `/applications`, or `/groups/{id}/members` endpoints with optional OData filtering, then applies sharding strategies (random, sequential, or percentage-based) to distribute results. Output shards are sets that can be directly used in conditional access policies, groups, and other resources requiring object ID collections.\n\nUnlike a datasource, this resource stores shard assignments in Terraform state. When `recalculate_on_next_run = false`, the stored assignments are returned unchanged on every plan and apply — preventing membership churn from causing reassignments. Set `recalculate_on_next_run = true` and run `terraform apply` to recompute shards from the current Graph API member list.\n\n**API Endpoints:** `GET /users`, `GET /devices`, `GET /applications`, `GET /groups/{id}/members` (with pagination and `ConsistencyLevel: eventual` header)\n\n**Common Use Cases:** MFA rollouts, Windows Update rings, conditional access pilots, application-based policies, group splitting, A/B testing","description_kind":"markdown"}}},"data_source_schemas":{"microsoft365_graph_beta_applications_application":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"api":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"accept_mapped_claims":{"type":"bool","description":"Allows an application to use claims mapping without specifying a custom signing key.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"known_client_applications":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"Used for bundling consent if you have a solution that contains two parts: a client app and a custom web API app. If you set the appID of the client app to this value, the user only consents once to the client app. Microsoft Entra ID knows that consenting to the client means implicitly consenting to the web API and automatically provisions service principals for both APIs at the same time. Both the client and the web API app must be registered in the same tenant.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"oauth2_permission_scopes":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"admin_consent_description":{"type":"string","description":"A description of the delegated permissions, intended to be read by an administrator granting the permission on behalf of all users. This text appears in tenant-wide admin consent experiences.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"admin_consent_display_name":{"type":"string","description":"The permission's title, intended to be read by an administrator granting the permission on behalf of all users.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"Unique scope permission identifier inside the oauth2PermissionScopes collection. Required.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"is_enabled":{"type":"bool","description":"When you create or update a permission, this property must be set to true (which is the default). To delete a permission, this property must first be set to false. At that point, in a subsequent call, the permission may be removed.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"type":{"type":"string","description":"The possible values are: `User` and `Admin`. Specifies whether this delegated permission should be considered safe for non-admin users to consent to on behalf of themselves, or whether an administrator consent should be required for the permissions. While Microsoft Graph defines the default consent requirement for each permission, the tenant administrator may override the behavior in their organization (by allowing, restricting, or limiting user consent to this delegated permission). For more information, see Configure how users consent to applications.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"user_consent_description":{"type":"string","description":"A description of the delegated permissions, intended to be read by a user granting the permission on their own behalf. This text appears in consent experiences where the user is consenting only on behalf of themselves.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"user_consent_display_name":{"type":"string","description":"A title for the permission, intended to be read by a user granting the permission on their own behalf. This text appears in consent experiences where the user is consenting only on behalf of themselves.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"value":{"type":"string","description":"Specifies the value to include in the scp (scope) claim in access tokens. Must not exceed 120 characters in length. Allowed characters are : ! # $ % \u0026 ' ( ) * + , - . / : ;  =  ? @ [ ] ^ + _  {  } ~, and characters in the ranges 0-9, A-Z and a-z. Any other character, including the space character, aren't allowed. May not begin with `.`.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"The definition of the delegated permissions exposed by the web API represented by this application registration. These delegated permissions may be requested by a client application, and may be granted by users or administrators during consent. Delegated permissions are sometimes referred to as OAuth 2.0 scopes.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"pre_authorized_applications":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"app_id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier for the client application.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"delegated_permission_ids":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"The unique identifier for the scopes the client application is granted.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"Lists the client applications that are preauthorized with the specified delegated permissions to access this application's APIs. Users aren't required to consent to any preauthorized application (for the permissions specified). However, any other permissions not listed in preAuthorizedApplications (requested through incremental consent for example) will require user consent.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"requested_access_token_version":{"type":"number","description":"Specifies the access token version expected by this resource. This changes the version and format of the JWT produced independent of the endpoint or client used to request the access token. The endpoint used, v1.0 or v2.0, is chosen by the client and only impacts the version of id_tokens. Resources need to explicitly configure requestedAccessTokenVersion to indicate the supported access token format. Possible values for requestedAccessTokenVersion are 1, 2, or null. If the value is null, this defaults to 1, which corresponds to the v1.0 endpoint. If signInAudience on the application is configured as AzureADandPersonalMicrosoftAccount or PersonalMicrosoftAccount, the value for this property must be 2.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Specifies settings for an application that implements a web API.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"app_id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier for the application that is assigned by Microsoft Entra ID. Not nullable. Read-only. Alternate key. Supports `$filter` (`eq`). One of `object_id`, `app_id`, `display_name`, or `odata_query` must be specified.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"app_roles":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"allowed_member_types":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"Specifies whether this app role can be assigned to users and groups (by setting to `['User']`), to other application's (by setting to `['Application']`, or both (by setting to `['User', 'Application']`). App roles supporting assignment to other applications' service principals are also known as application permissions. The 'Application' value is only supported for app roles defined on application entities. Required.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"description":{"type":"string","description":"The description for the app role. This is displayed when the app role is being assigned and, if the app role functions as an application permission, during consent experiences. Required.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"Display name for the permission that appears in the app role assignment and consent experiences. Required.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"Unique role identifier inside the appRoles collection. When creating a new app role, a new GUID identifier must be provided. Required.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"is_enabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Defines whether the application's app role is enabled or disabled. Required.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"origin":{"type":"string","description":"Specifies if the app role is defined on the application object or on the servicePrincipal entity. Must not be included in any POST or PATCH requests. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"value":{"type":"string","description":"Specifies the value to include in the roles claim in ID tokens and access tokens authenticating an assigned user or service principal. Must not exceed 120 characters in length. Allowed characters are : ! # $ % \u0026 ' ( ) * + , - . / : ;  =  ? @ [ ] ^ + _  {  } ~, and characters in the ranges 0-9, A-Z and a-z. Any other character, including the space character, aren't allowed. May not begin with `.`. Nullable.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"The collection of roles defined for the application. With app role assignments, these roles can be assigned to users, groups, or service principals associated with other applications. Not nullable.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"created_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time the application was registered. The DateTimeOffset type represents date and time information using ISO 8601 format and is always in UTC time. For example, midnight UTC on Jan 1, 2014 is 2014-01-01T00:00:00Z. Read-only. Supports `$filter` (`eq`, `ne`, `not`, `ge`, `le`, `in`, and `eq` on null values) and `$orderby`.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"deleted_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time the application was deleted. The DateTimeOffset type represents date and time information using ISO 8601 format and is always in UTC time. For example, midnight UTC on Jan 1, 2014 is 2014-01-01T00:00:00Z. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"description":{"type":"string","description":"Free text field to provide a description of the application object to end users. The maximum allowed size is 1,024 characters. Returned by default. Supports `$filter` (`eq`, `ne`, `not`, `ge`, `le`, `startsWith`) and `$search`.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"disabled_by_microsoft_status":{"type":"string","description":"Specifies whether Microsoft has disabled the registered application. The possible values are: null (default value), `NotDisabled`, and `DisabledDueToViolationOfServicesAgreement` (reasons may include suspicious, abusive, or malicious activity, or a violation of the Microsoft Services Agreement). Supports `$filter` (`eq`, `ne`, `not`). Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"The display name for the application. Maximum length is 256 characters. Supports `$filter` (`eq`, `ne`, `not`, `ge`, `le`, `in`, `startsWith`, and `eq` on null values), `$search`, and `$orderby`. One of `object_id`, `app_id`, `display_name`, or `odata_query` must be specified.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"group_membership_claims":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"Configures the groups claim issued in a user or OAuth 2.0 access token that the application expects. To set this attribute, use one of the following string values: `None`, `SecurityGroup` (for security groups and Microsoft Entra roles), `All` (this gets all security groups, distribution groups, and Microsoft Entra directory roles that the signed-in user is a member of).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"Unique identifier for the application object. This property is referred to as **Object ID** in the Microsoft Entra admin center. Key. Not nullable. Read-only. Supports `$filter` (`eq`, `ne`, `not`, `in`).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"identifier_uris":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"Also known as App ID URI, this value is set when an application is used as a resource app. The identifierUris acts as the prefix for the scopes you reference in your API's code, and it must be globally unique across Microsoft Entra ID. For more information on valid identifierUris patterns and best practices, see Microsoft Entra application registration security best practices. Not nullable. Supports `$filter` (`eq`, `ne`, `ge`, `le`, `startsWith`).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"info":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"logo_url":{"type":"string","description":"CDN URL to the application's logo. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"marketing_url":{"type":"string","description":"Link to the application's marketing page. For example, https://www.contoso.com/app/marketing.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"privacy_statement_url":{"type":"string","description":"Link to the application's privacy statement. For example, https://www.contoso.com/app/privacy.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"support_url":{"type":"string","description":"Link to the application's support page. For example, https://www.contoso.com/app/support.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"terms_of_service_url":{"type":"string","description":"Link to the application's terms of service statement. For example, https://www.contoso.com/app/termsofservice.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Basic profile information of the application, such as it's marketing, support, terms of service, and privacy statement URLs. The terms of service and privacy statement are surfaced to users through the user consent experience. For more information, see How to: Add Terms of service and privacy statement for registered Microsoft Entra apps. Supports `$filter` (`eq`, `ne`, `not`, `ge`, `le`, and `eq` on null values).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"is_device_only_auth_supported":{"type":"bool","description":"Specifies whether this application supports device authentication without a user. The default is false.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"is_fallback_public_client":{"type":"bool","description":"Specifies the fallback application type as public client, such as an installed application running on a mobile device. The default value is false, which means the fallback application type is confidential client such as a web app. There are certain scenarios where Microsoft Entra ID can't determine the client application type. For example, the ROPC flow where the application is configured without specifying a redirect URI. In those cases Microsoft Entra ID interprets the application type based on the value of this property.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"key_credentials":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"custom_key_identifier":{"type":"string","description":"A 40-character binary type that can be used to identify the credential. Optional. When not provided in the payload, defaults to the thumbprint of the certificate.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"Friendly name for the key. Optional.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"end_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time at which the credential expires. The DateTimeOffset type represents date and time information using ISO 8601 format and is always in UTC time. For example, midnight UTC on Jan 1, 2014 is 2014-01-01T00:00:00Z.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"key":{"type":"string","description":"Value for the key credential. Should be a Base64 encoded value. Returned only on $select for a single object, that is, GET applications/{applicationId}?$select=keyCredentials or GET servicePrincipals/{servicePrincipalId}?$select=keyCredentials; otherwise, it's always null. From a .cer certificate, you can read the key using the Convert.ToBase64String() method. For more information, see Get the certificate key.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true,"sensitive":true},"key_id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier (GUID) for the key.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"start_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time at which the credential becomes valid. The DateTimeOffset type represents date and time information using ISO 8601 format and is always in UTC time. For example, midnight UTC on Jan 1, 2014 is 2014-01-01T00:00:00Z.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"type":{"type":"string","description":"The type of key credential; for example, `Symmetric`, `AsymmetricX509Cert`, or `X509CertAndPassword`.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"usage":{"type":"string","description":"A string that describes the purpose for which the key can be used; for example, `None​`, `Verify`, `PairwiseIdentifier`, `Sign`.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"The collection of key credentials associated with the application. This is a read-only attribute. To manage certificate credentials, use the `microsoft365_graph_beta_applications_application_certificate_credential` resource instead.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"notes":{"type":"string","description":"Notes relevant for the management of the application.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"object_id":{"type":"string","description":"The object ID of the application. One of `object_id`, `app_id`, `display_name`, or `odata_query` must be specified.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"odata_query":{"type":"string","description":"Custom OData filter query. Use this for advanced filtering when the standard lookup attributes don't meet your needs. Cannot be combined with `object_id`, `app_id`, or `display_name`. Example: `displayName eq 'My Application' and signInAudience eq 'AzureADMyOrg'`","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"optional_claims":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"access_token":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"additional_properties":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"Additional properties of the claim. If a property exists in this collection, it modifies the behavior of the optional claim specified in the name property.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"essential":{"type":"bool","description":"If the value is true, the claim specified by the client is necessary to ensure a smooth authorization experience for the specific task requested by the end user. The default value is false.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"name":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the optional claim. Required.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"source":{"type":"string","description":"The source (directory object) of the claim. There are predefined claims and user-defined claims from extension properties. If the source value is null, the claim is a predefined optional claim. If the source value is user, the value in the name property is the extension property from the user object.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"The optional claims returned in the JWT access token.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"id_token":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"additional_properties":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"Additional properties of the claim. If a property exists in this collection, it modifies the behavior of the optional claim specified in the name property.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"essential":{"type":"bool","description":"If the value is true, the claim specified by the client is necessary to ensure a smooth authorization experience for the specific task requested by the end user. The default value is false.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"name":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the optional claim. Required.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"source":{"type":"string","description":"The source (directory object) of the claim. There are predefined claims and user-defined claims from extension properties. If the source value is null, the claim is a predefined optional claim. If the source value is user, the value in the name property is the extension property from the user object.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"The optional claims returned in the JWT ID token.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"saml2_token":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"additional_properties":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"Additional properties of the claim. If a property exists in this collection, it modifies the behavior of the optional claim specified in the name property.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"essential":{"type":"bool","description":"If the value is true, the claim specified by the client is necessary to ensure a smooth authorization experience for the specific task requested by the end user. The default value is false.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"name":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the optional claim. Required.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"source":{"type":"string","description":"The source (directory object) of the claim. There are predefined claims and user-defined claims from extension properties. If the source value is null, the claim is a predefined optional claim. If the source value is user, the value in the name property is the extension property from the user object.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"The optional claims returned in the SAML token.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Application developers can configure optional claims in their Microsoft Entra applications to specify the claims that are sent to their application by the Microsoft security token service. For more information, see How to: Provide optional claims to your app.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"owner_user_ids":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"The user IDs of the owners for the application. At least one owner is typically required when creating an application. Owners are a set of non-admin users or service principals allowed to modify this object.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"parental_control_settings":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"countries_blocked_for_minors":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"Specifies the two-letter ISO country codes. Access to the application will be blocked for minors from the countries specified in this list.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"legal_age_group_rule":{"type":"string","description":"Specifies the legal age group rule that applies to users of the app. Can be set to one of the following values: `Allow`, `RequireConsentForPrivacyServices`, `RequireConsentForMinors`, `RequireConsentForKids`, `BlockMinors`.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Specifies parental control settings for an application.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"password_credentials":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"custom_key_identifier":{"type":"string","description":"Do not use.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"Friendly name for the password. Optional.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"end_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time at which the password expires represented using ISO 8601 format and is always in UTC time. For example, midnight UTC on Jan 1, 2014 is 2014-01-01T00:00:00Z. Optional.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"hint":{"type":"string","description":"Contains the first three characters of the password. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"key_id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier for the password. Required.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"secret_text":{"type":"string","description":"Read-only; Contains the strong passwords generated by Microsoft Entra ID that are 16-64 characters in length. The generated password value is only returned during the initial POST request to addPassword. There is no way to retrieve this password in the future.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true,"sensitive":true},"start_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time at which the password becomes valid. The Timestamp type represents date and time information using ISO 8601 format and is always in UTC time. For example, midnight UTC on Jan 1, 2014 is 2014-01-01T00:00:00Z. Optional.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"The collection of password credentials associated with the application. Not nullable.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"public_client":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"redirect_uris":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"Specifies the URLs where user tokens are sent for sign-in, or the redirect URIs where OAuth 2.0 authorization codes and access tokens are sent.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Specifies settings for installed clients such as desktop or mobile devices.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"publisher_domain":{"type":"string","description":"The verified publisher domain for the application. Read-only. Supports `$filter` (`eq`, `ne`, `ge`, `le`, `startsWith`).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"required_resource_access":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"resource_access":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier of an app role or delegated permission exposed by the resource application. For delegated permissions, this should match the id property of one of the delegated permissions in the oauth2PermissionScopes collection of the resource application's service principal. For app roles (application permissions), this should match the id property of an app role in the appRoles collection of the resource application's service principal. Required.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"type":{"type":"string","description":"Specifies whether the id property references a delegated permission or an app role (application permission). The possible values are: `Scope` (for delegated permissions) or `Role` (for app roles). Required.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"The list of OAuth2.0 permission scopes and app roles that the application requires from the specified resource. Required.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"resource_app_id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier for the resource that the application requires access to. This should be equal to the appId declared on the target resource application. Required.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"Specifies the resources that the application needs to access. This property also specifies the set of delegated permissions and application roles that it needs for each of those resources. This configuration of access to the required resources drives the consent experience. No more than 50 resource services (APIs) can be configured. Beginning mid-October 2021, the total number of required permissions must not exceed 400. For more information, see Limits on requested permissions per app. Not nullable. Supports `$filter` (`eq`, `not`, `ge`, `le`).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"service_management_reference":{"type":"string","description":"References application or service contact information from a Service or Asset Management database. Nullable.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"sign_in_audience":{"type":"string","description":"Specifies the Microsoft accounts that are supported for the current application. The possible values are: `AzureADMyOrg` (default), `AzureADMultipleOrgs`, `AzureADandPersonalMicrosoftAccount`, and `PersonalMicrosoftAccount`. The value of this object also limits the number of permissions an app can request. For more information, see Limits on requested permissions per app. The value for this property has implications on other app object properties. As a result, if you change this property, you may need to change other properties first. For more information, see Validation differences for signInAudience. Supports `$filter` (`eq`, `ne`, `not`).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"sign_in_audience_restrictions":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"allowed_tenant_ids":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"The list of allowed tenant IDs. Only applicable when odata_type is `#microsoft.graph.allowedTenantsAudience`.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"is_home_tenant_allowed":{"type":"bool","description":"Indicates whether the home tenant is allowed. Only applicable when odata_type is `#microsoft.graph.allowedTenantsAudience`.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"odata_type":{"type":"string","description":"The OData type. Must be `#microsoft.graph.allowedTenantsAudience` or `#microsoft.graph.unrestrictedAudience`.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Specifies restrictions on the supported account types specified in signInAudience. The value type determines the restrictions that can be applied: unrestrictedAudience (There are no additional restrictions on the supported account types allowed by signInAudience) or allowedTenantsAudience (The application can only be used in the specified Entra tenants. Only supported when signInAudience is AzureADMultipleOrgs). Default is a value of type unrestrictedAudience. Returned only on `$select`.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"spa":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"redirect_uris":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"Specifies the URLs where user tokens are sent for sign-in, or the redirect URIs where OAuth 2.0 authorization codes and access tokens are sent.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Specifies settings for a single-page application, including sign out URLs and redirect URIs for authorization codes and access tokens.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"tags":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"Custom strings that can be used to categorize and identify the application. Not nullable. Strings added here also appear in the tags property of any associated service principals. Supports `$filter` (`eq`, `not`, `ge`, `le`, `startsWith`) and `$search`.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"web":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"home_page_url":{"type":"string","description":"Home page or landing page of the application.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"implicit_grant_settings":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"enable_access_token_issuance":{"type":"bool","description":"Specifies whether this web application can request an access token using the OAuth 2.0 implicit flow.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"enable_id_token_issuance":{"type":"bool","description":"Specifies whether this web application can request an ID token using the OAuth 2.0 implicit flow.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Specifies whether this web application can request tokens using the OAuth 2.0 implicit flow.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"logout_url":{"type":"string","description":"Specifies the URL that is used by Microsoft's authorization service to log out a user using front-channel, back-channel or SAML logout protocols.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"redirect_uri_settings":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"index":{"type":"number","description":"Identifies the specific URI within the redirectURIs collection in SAML SSO flows. Defaults to null. The index is unique across all the redirectUris for the application.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"uri":{"type":"string","description":"Specifies the URI that tokens are sent to.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"set"},"description":"Specifies the index of the URLs where user tokens are sent for sign-in. This is only valid for applications using SAML. Note: If not specified, the API may auto-generate settings based on redirect_uris. To manage this field, you must provide at least one entry; empty arrays are not supported as the API auto-generates values.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"redirect_uris":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"Specifies the URLs where user tokens are sent for sign-in, or the redirect URIs where OAuth 2.0 authorization codes and access tokens are sent.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Specifies settings for a web application.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"description":"Retrieves information about a Microsoft Entra ID (Azure AD) application using the `/applications` endpoint. This data source is used to query application details by ID, app ID, display name, or advanced OData filtering.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_applications_service_principal":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"account_enabled":{"type":"bool","description":"true if the service principal account is enabled; otherwise, false. If set to false, then no users are able to sign in to this app, even if they're assigned to it. Supports `$filter` (`eq`, `ne`, `not`, `in`).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"app_display_name":{"type":"string","description":"The display name exposed by the associated application.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"app_id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier for the associated application (client ID). Not nullable. Read-only. Alternate key. Supports `$filter` (`eq`). One of `object_id`, `app_id`, `display_name`, or `odata_query` must be specified.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"app_owner_organization_id":{"type":"string","description":"Contains the tenant ID where the application is registered. This is applicable only to service principals backed by applications. Supports `$filter` (`eq`, `ne`, `NOT`, `ge`, `le`).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"app_role_assignment_required":{"type":"bool","description":"Specifies whether users or other service principals need to be granted an app role assignment for this service principal before users can sign in or apps can get tokens. The default value is false. Not nullable. Supports `$filter` (`eq`, `ne`, `NOT`).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"application_template_id":{"type":"string","description":"Unique identifier of the applicationTemplate that the servicePrincipal was created from. Read-only. Supports `$filter` (`eq`, `ne`, `NOT`, `startsWith`).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"deleted_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time the service principal was deleted. The DateTimeOffset type represents date and time information using ISO 8601 format and is always in UTC time. For example, midnight UTC on Jan 1, 2014 is 2014-01-01T00:00:00Z. Read-only.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"disabled_by_microsoft_status":{"type":"string","description":"Specifies whether Microsoft has disabled the registered application. Possible values are: `null` (default value), `NotDisabled`, and `DisabledDueToViolationOfServicesAgreement` (reasons include suspicious, abusive, or malicious activity, or a violation of the Microsoft Services Agreement). Supports `$filter` (`eq`, `ne`, `NOT`).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"The display name for the service principal. Supports `$filter` (`eq`, `ne`, `not`, `ge`, `le`, `in`, `startsWith`, and `eq` on null values), `$search`, and `$orderby`. One of `object_id`, `app_id`, `display_name`, or `odata_query` must be specified.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"error_url":{"type":"string","description":"Deprecated. Do not use.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"homepage":{"type":"string","description":"Home page or landing page of the application.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"Unique identifier for the service principal object. This property is referred to as **Object ID** in the Microsoft Entra admin center. Key. Not nullable. Read-only. Supports `$filter` (`eq`, `ne`, `not`, `in`).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"info":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"logo_url":{"type":"string","description":"CDN URL to the application's logo.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"marketing_url":{"type":"string","description":"Link to the application's marketing page.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"privacy_statement_url":{"type":"string","description":"Link to the application's privacy statement.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"support_url":{"type":"string","description":"Link to the application's support page.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"terms_of_service_url":{"type":"string","description":"Link to the application's terms of service statement.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Basic profile information of the acquired application such as app's marketing, support, terms of service and privacy statement URLs. The terms of service and privacy statement are surfaced to users through the user consent experience. For more information, see How to: Add Terms of service and privacy statement for registered Azure AD apps.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"login_url":{"type":"string","description":"Specifies the URL where the service provider redirects the user to Azure AD to authenticate. Azure AD uses the URL to launch the application from Microsoft 365 or the Azure AD My Apps. When blank, Azure AD performs IdP-initiated sign-on for applications configured with SAML-based single sign-on.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"logout_url":{"type":"string","description":"Specifies the URL that the Microsoft's authorization service uses to sign out a user using OpenId Connect front-channel, back-channel, or SAML sign out protocols.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"notes":{"type":"string","description":"Free text field to capture information about the service principal, typically used for operational purposes. Maximum allowed size is 1,024 characters.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"notification_email_addresses":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"Specifies the list of email addresses where Azure AD sends a notification when the active certificate is near the expiration date. This is only for the certificates used to sign the SAML token issued for Azure AD Gallery applications.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"object_id":{"type":"string","description":"The object ID of the service principal. One of `object_id`, `app_id`, `display_name`, or `odata_query` must be specified.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"odata_query":{"type":"string","description":"Custom OData filter query. Use this for advanced filtering when the standard lookup attributes don't meet your needs. Cannot be combined with `object_id`, `app_id`, or `display_name`. Example: `displayName eq 'My Service Principal' and servicePrincipalType eq 'Application'`","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"preferred_single_sign_on_mode":{"type":"string","description":"Specifies the single sign-on mode configured for this application. Azure AD uses the preferred single sign-on mode to launch the application from Microsoft 365 or the Azure AD My Apps. The supported values are `password`, `saml`, `notSupported`, and `oidc`.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"preferred_token_signing_key_end_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"Specifies the expiration date of the keyCredential used for token signing, marked by preferredTokenSigningKeyThumbprint. Updating this attribute isn't currently supported. For details, see ServicePrincipal property differences. The Timestamp type represents date and time information using ISO 8601 format and is always in UTC time.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"preferred_token_signing_key_thumbprint":{"type":"string","description":"This property can be used on SAML applications (apps that have preferredSingleSignOnMode set to saml) to control which certificate is used to sign the SAML responses. For applications that aren't SAML, don't write or otherwise rely on this property.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"publisher_name":{"type":"string","description":"The display name of the tenant in which the associated application is registered. Provided only when the application publisher is from a different tenant. Supports `$filter` (`eq`, `ne`, `ge`, `le`, `startsWith`).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"reply_urls":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"The URLs that user tokens are sent to for sign in with the associated application, or the redirect URIs that OAuth 2.0 authorization codes and access tokens are sent to for the associated application. Not nullable.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"saml_metadata_url":{"type":"string","description":"The URL where the service exposes SAML metadata for federation.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"saml_single_sign_on_settings":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"relay_state":{"type":"string","description":"The relative URI the service provider would redirect to after completion of the single sign-on flow.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"The collection for settings related to saml single sign-on.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"service_principal_names":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"Contains the list of identifiersUris, copied over from the associated application. More values can be added to hybrid applications. These values can be used to identify the permissions exposed by this app within Azure AD. Supports `$filter` (`eq`, `ne`, `ge`, `le`, `startsWith`).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"service_principal_type":{"type":"string","description":"Identifies if the service principal represents an Application, a ManagedIdentity, or a legacy application (socialIdp). This is set by Azure AD internally. For a service principal that represents an Application this is set as Application. For a service principal that represent a managed identity this is set as ManagedIdentity. For a service principal representing a legacy app this is set as SocialIdp. Supports `$filter` (`eq`, `ne`, `NOT`, `in`).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"sign_in_audience":{"type":"string","description":"Specifies the Microsoft accounts that are supported for the current application. Supported values are `AzureADMyOrg`, `AzureADMultipleOrgs`, `AzureADandPersonalMicrosoftAccount`, `PersonalMicrosoftAccount`. Read-only. Supports `$filter` (`eq`, `ne`, `NOT`, `startsWith`).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"tags":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"Custom strings that can be used to categorize and identify the service principal. Not nullable. Supports `$filter` (`eq`, `ne`, `NOT`, `ge`, `le`, `startsWith`).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"verified_publisher":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"added_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The timestamp when the verified publisher was first added or most recently updated.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"The verified publisher name from the app publisher's Microsoft Partner Network (MPN) account.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"verified_publisher_id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the verified publisher from the app publisher's Partner Center account.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Specifies the verified publisher of the application which this service principal represents.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"description":"Retrieves information about a Microsoft Entra ID service principal using the `/servicePrincipals` endpoint. This data source is used to query enterprise applications and managed identities by ID, app ID, display name, or advanced OData filtering.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_device_and_app_management_application_category":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"filter_type":{"type":"string","description":"Type of filter to apply. Valid values are: `all`, `id`, `display_name`, `odata`.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"filter_value":{"type":"string","description":"Value to filter by. Required when filter_type is 'id' or 'display_name'. Not required when filter_type is 'all' or 'odata'.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"items":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"The display name of the application category.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier of the application category.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"last_modified_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time when the application category was last modified in RFC3339 format.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"list"},"description":"The list of application categories that match the filter criteria.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"odata_filter":{"type":"string","description":"OData filter query. Only used when filter_type is 'odata'. Supports standard OData filter syntax (e.g., `displayName eq 'Finance'`, `startswith(displayName, 'IT')`).","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"odata_top":{"type":"number","description":"OData $top parameter to limit the number of results. Only used when filter_type is 'odata'.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"Retrieves application categories from Microsoft Intune using the `/deviceAppManagement/mobileAppCategories` endpoint. This data source is used to query organizational app categories for classifying and organizing mobile applications.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_device_and_app_management_mobile_app":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"app_id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier of the mobile app. Conflicts with other lookup attributes.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"app_type_filter":{"type":"string","description":"Optional filter that filters returned apps by the application type. Supported values are: `macOSPkgApp`, `macOSDmgApp`, `macOSLobApp`, `macOSMicrosoftDefenderApp`, `macOSMicrosoftEdgeApp`, `macOSOfficeSuiteApp`, `macOsVppApp`, `macOSWebClip`, `androidForWorkApp`, `androidLobApp`, `androidManagedStoreApp`, `androidManagedStoreWebApp`, `androidStoreApp`, `managedAndroidLobApp`, `managedAndroidStoreApp`, `iosiPadOSWebClip`, `iosLobApp`, `iosStoreApp`, `iosVppApp`, `managedIOSLobApp`, `managedIOSStoreApp`, `windowsAppX`, `windowsMicrosoftEdgeApp`, `windowsMobileMSI`, `windowsPhone81AppX`, `windowsPhone81AppXBundle`, `windowsPhone81StoreApp`, `windowsPhoneXAP`, `windowsStoreApp`, `windowsUniversalAppX`, `windowsWebApp`, `winGetApp`, `webApp`, `microsoftStoreForBusinessApp`, `officeSuiteApp`, `win32CatalogApp`, `win32LobApp`, `managedApp`, `managedMobileLobApp`, `mobileLobApp`.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"category":{"type":"string","description":"Filter apps by category name (case-insensitive partial match). Conflicts with other lookup attributes.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"developer":{"type":"string","description":"Filter apps by developer name (case-insensitive partial match). Conflicts with other lookup attributes.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"Filter apps by display name (case-insensitive partial match). Conflicts with other lookup attributes.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"items":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"categories":{"type":["list","string"],"description":"The list of categories for this app.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"created_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time the app was created.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"dependent_app_count":{"type":"number","description":"The total number of dependencies the child app has.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"description":{"type":"string","description":"The description of the app.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"developer":{"type":"string","description":"The developer of the app.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"The admin provided or imported title of the app.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"Key of the entity.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"information_url":{"type":"string","description":"The more information Url.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"is_assigned":{"type":"bool","description":"The value indicating whether the app is assigned to at least one group.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"is_featured":{"type":"bool","description":"The value indicating whether the app is marked as featured by the admin.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"last_modified_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time the app was last modified.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"notes":{"type":"string","description":"Notes for the app.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"owner":{"type":"string","description":"The owner of the app.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"privacy_information_url":{"type":"string","description":"The privacy statement Url.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"publisher":{"type":"string","description":"The publisher of the app.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"publishing_state":{"type":"string","description":"The publishing state for the app. The app cannot be assigned unless the app is published. Possible values are: `notPublished`, `processing`, `published`.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"role_scope_tag_ids":{"type":["list","string"],"description":"List of scope tag ids for this mobile app.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"superseded_app_count":{"type":"number","description":"The total number of apps this app is directly or indirectly superseded by.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"superseding_app_count":{"type":"number","description":"The total number of apps this app directly or indirectly supersedes.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"upload_state":{"type":"number","description":"The upload state.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"list"},"description":"The list of mobile apps that match the filter criteria.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"list_all":{"type":"bool","description":"Retrieve all mobile apps. Conflicts with specific lookup attributes.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"odata_query":{"type":"string","description":"Custom OData filter expression for advanced filtering. Example: `startswith(publisher, 'Microsoft') and isAssigned eq true`. Conflicts with other lookup attributes.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"publisher":{"type":"string","description":"Filter apps by publisher name (case-insensitive partial match). Conflicts with other lookup attributes.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"Retrieves mobile applications from Microsoft Intune using the `/deviceAppManagement/mobileApps` endpoint. Supports flexible lookup by app ID, display name, publisher, developer, category, or custom OData queries.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_device_and_app_management_mobile_app_catalog_package":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"filter_type":{"type":"string","description":"Type of filter to apply. Valid values are: `all`, `id`, `product_name`, `publisher_name`, `odata`.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"fi