n](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"Retrieves Cloud PC frontline service plans from Microsoft Intune using the `/deviceManagement/virtualEndpoint/frontlineServicePlans` endpoint. This data source is used to query shared Cloud PC plans and their capacity utilization.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_windows_365_cloud_pc_gallery_image":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"filter_type":{"type":"string","description":"Type of filter to apply. Valid values are: `all`, `id`, `display_name`. Use 'all' to retrieve all gallery images, 'id' to retrieve a specific image by its unique identifier, or 'display_name' to filter by the image's display name.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"filter_value":{"type":"string","description":"Value to filter by. Not required when filter_type is 'all'. For 'id', provide the gallery image ID. For 'display_name', provide a substring to match against image display names.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"items":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"The display name of this gallery image. For example, Windows 11 Enterprise + Microsoft 365 Apps 22H2.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"end_date":{"type":"string","description":"The date when the status of image becomes supportedWithWarning.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"expiration_date":{"type":"string","description":"The date when the image is no longer available. Users are unable to provision new Cloud PCs if the current time is later than this date.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier (ID) of the gallery image resource on Cloud PC. The ID format is {publisherName_offerName_skuName}.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"offer_name":{"type":"string","description":"The offer name of this gallery image that is passed to ARM to retrieve the image resource.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"os_version_number":{"type":"string","description":"The operating system version of this gallery image. For example, 10.0.22000.296.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"publisher_name":{"type":"string","description":"The publisher name of this gallery image that is passed to ARM to retrieve the image resource.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"size_in_gb":{"type":"number","description":"Indicates the size of this image in gigabytes. For example, 64.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"sku_name":{"type":"string","description":"The SKU name of this image that is passed to ARM to retrieve the image resource.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"start_date":{"type":"string","description":"The date when the Cloud PC image is available for provisioning new Cloud PCs.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"status":{"type":"string","description":"The status of the gallery image on the Cloud PC. Possible values are: supported, supportedWithWarning, notSupported, unknownFutureValue.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"list"},"description":"The list of Cloud PC gallery images that match the filter criteria.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"Retrieves Cloud PC gallery images from Microsoft Intune using the `/deviceManagement/virtualEndpoint/galleryImages` endpoint. This data source is used to discover Microsoft-provided OS images with their support status and version details.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_windows_365_cloud_pc_source_device_image":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"filter_type":{"type":"string","description":"Type of filter to apply. Valid values are: `all`, `id`, `display_name`. Use 'all' to retrieve all images, 'id' to retrieve a specific image by its unique identifier, or 'display_name' to filter by the image's display name.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"filter_value":{"type":"string","description":"Value to filter by. Not required when filter_type is 'all'. For 'id', provide the image ID. For 'display_name', provide a substring to match against image display names.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"items":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"The display name of the source device image.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier for the source device image.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"resource_id":{"type":"string","description":"The resource ID for the source device image.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"subscription_display_name":{"type":"string","description":"The display name of the subscription.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"subscription_id":{"type":"string","description":"The subscription ID associated with the image.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"list"},"description":"The list of Cloud PC source device images that match the filter criteria.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"Retrieves Cloud PC source device images from Microsoft Intune using the `/deviceManagement/virtualEndpoint/deviceImages/getSourceImages` endpoint. This data source is used to discover available Azure images for uploading and provisioning Cloud PCs with filtering options.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_windows_365_cloud_pcs":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"filter_type":{"type":"string","description":"Type of filter to apply. Valid values are: `all`, `id`, `display_name`, `odata`. Use 'all' to retrieve all Cloud PCs, 'id' to retrieve a specific Cloud PC by its unique identifier, 'display_name' to filter by name, or 'odata' to use advanced OData query parameters.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"filter_value":{"type":"string","description":"Value to filter by. Not required when filter_type is 'all'. For 'id', provide the Cloud PC ID. For other filters, provide the appropriate value to match.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"items":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"aad_device_id":{"type":"string","description":"The Azure AD device ID associated with the Cloud PC.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"device_region_name":{"type":"string","description":"The Azure region where the Cloud PC is deployed.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"disk_encryption_state":{"type":"string","description":"The disk encryption state of the Cloud PC (e.g., encryptedUsingPlatformManagedKey).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"The display name of the Cloud PC.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"enable_single_sign_on":{"type":"bool","description":"Indicates whether single sign-on is enabled for the Cloud PC.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"grace_period_end_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time when the grace period for the Cloud PC ends.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier for the Cloud PC.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"image_display_name":{"type":"string","description":"The display name of the image used for the Cloud PC.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"last_modified_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time when the Cloud PC was last modified.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"managed_device_id":{"type":"string","description":"The managed device ID associated with the Cloud PC.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"managed_device_name":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the managed device associated with the Cloud PC.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"on_premises_connection_name":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the on-premises connection used for the Cloud PC.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"product_type":{"type":"string","description":"The product type of the Cloud PC (e.g., enterprise).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"provisioning_policy_id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the provisioning policy used for the Cloud PC.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"provisioning_policy_name":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the provisioning policy used for the Cloud PC.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"provisioning_type":{"type":"string","description":"The type of provisioning used for the Cloud PC (e.g., dedicated).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"service_plan_id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the service plan associated with the Cloud PC.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"service_plan_name":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the service plan associated with the Cloud PC.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"service_plan_type":{"type":"string","description":"The type of service plan associated with the Cloud PC.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"status":{"type":"string","description":"The current status of the Cloud PC (e.g., provisioned, provisioning, failed).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"status_detail_code":{"type":"string","description":"The error/warning code associated with the Cloud PC status.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"status_detail_message":{"type":"string","description":"The status message associated with the error code.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"user_account_type":{"type":"string","description":"The account type of the user on provisioned Cloud PCs (e.g., standardUser, administrator).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"user_principal_name":{"type":"string","description":"The user principal name (UPN) of the user assigned to the Cloud PC.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"list"},"description":"The list of Cloud PCs that match the filter criteria.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"odata_count":{"type":"bool","description":"OData $count query parameter to include a count of items. Only applicable when filter_type is 'odata'.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"odata_filter":{"type":"string","description":"OData $filter query parameter. Only applicable when filter_type is 'odata'. Example: \"status eq 'provisioned'\"","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"odata_select":{"type":"string","description":"OData $select query parameter to specify which fields to return. Only applicable when filter_type is 'odata'. Example: \"id,displayName,status\"","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"odata_top":{"type":"number","description":"OData $top query parameter to limit the number of items returned. Only applicable when filter_type is 'odata'.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"Retrieves Cloud PCs from Microsoft Intune using the `/deviceManagement/virtualEndpoint/cloudPCs` endpoint. This data source is used to query Cloud PCs with advanced filtering capabilities.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_windows_updates_applicable_content":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"applicable_content":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"catalog_entry":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"deployable_until_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time until which the driver can be deployed, in RFC3339 format.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"description":{"type":"string","description":"Description of the driver update.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"The display name of the driver update.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"driver_class":{"type":"string","description":"The class of the driver, e.g., 'Display', 'Network'.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier for the driver update catalog entry.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"manufacturer":{"type":"string","description":"The manufacturer of the driver.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"provider":{"type":"string","description":"The provider of the driver update.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"release_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The release date and time in RFC3339 format.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"version":{"type":"string","description":"The version of the driver.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"version_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The version date and time in RFC3339 format.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Details about the driver update catalog entry.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"catalog_entry_id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the catalog entry for this applicable content.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"matched_devices":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"device_id":{"type":"string","description":"The Azure AD device ID.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"recommended_by":{"type":["list","string"],"description":"List of entities recommending this driver, e.g., ['Microsoft', 'Contoso'].","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"list"},"description":"List of devices that match this driver update.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"list"},"description":"List of applicable content entries (drivers/firmware) for the audience.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"audience_id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the deployment audience to query for applicable content. This is required as applicable content is scoped to a specific audience.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"catalog_entry_type":{"type":"string","description":"Optional filter to only return content of a specific type. Valid values: `driver`, `quality`, `feature`. When specified, only catalog entries of this type will be returned.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"device_id":{"type":"string","description":"Optional Azure AD device ID to filter results. When specified, only shows applicable content that matches this specific device.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"driver_class":{"type":"string","description":"Optional filter to only return driver updates of a specific class. Examples: `Display`, `Network`, `Storage`, `Audio`, `Bluetooth`. Only applicable when filtering for driver updates.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"include_no_matches":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether to include content with no matched devices. Defaults to `true`. Set to `false` to only return content that has at least one matched device.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"manufacturer":{"type":"string","description":"Optional filter to only return updates from a specific manufacturer. Examples: `Intel`, `NVIDIA`, `AMD`, `Microsoft`, `Realtek`.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"odata_filter":{"type":"string","description":"Optional custom OData filter expression for advanced filtering. This is applied client-side after retrieving the applicable content. Example: `catalogEntry/displayName contains 'NVIDIA'`.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"Retrieves applicable content (driver and firmware updates) for a deployment audience using the `/admin/windows/updates/deploymentAudiences/{audienceId}/applicableContent` endpoint. This data source shows which updates are applicable to devices in a deployment audience, along with which devices match each update. Supports filtering by catalog entry type, driver class, manufacturer, and specific devices.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_windows_updates_catalog_enteries":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"entries":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"catalog_entry_type":{"type":"string","description":"The type of catalog entry. Values: 'featureUpdate' or 'qualityUpdate'.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"catalog_name":{"type":"string","description":"The catalog name of the quality update (quality updates only).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"cve_severity_information":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"exploited_cves":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"number":{"type":"string","description":"The CVE number, e.g., 'CVE-2023-32046'.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"url":{"type":"string","description":"The URL to the CVE details.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"list"},"description":"List of exploited CVEs.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"max_base_score":{"type":"number","description":"The maximum CVSS base score.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"max_severity":{"type":"string","description":"The maximum severity level of CVEs, e.g., 'critical'.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"CVE severity information for the quality update (quality updates only).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"deployable_until_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time until which the update can be deployed, in RFC3339 format. Null if no expiration.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"The display name of the catalog entry.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier for the catalog entry.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"is_expeditable":{"type":"bool","description":"Indicates whether the quality update can be expedited (quality updates only).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"quality_update_cadence":{"type":"string","description":"The release cadence of the quality update, e.g., 'monthly' (quality updates only).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"quality_update_classification":{"type":"string","description":"The classification of the quality update, e.g., 'security' (quality updates only).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"release_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The release date and time of the catalog entry in RFC3339 format.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"short_name":{"type":"string","description":"The short name of the quality update (quality updates only).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"version":{"type":"string","description":"The version of the feature update (feature updates only).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"list"},"description":"The list of Windows Update Catalog Entries that match the filter criteria.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"filter_type":{"type":"string","description":"Type of filter to apply. Valid values are: `all`, `id`, `display_name`, `catalog_entry_type`.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"filter_value":{"type":"string","description":"Value to filter by. Not required when filter_type is 'all'. For catalog_entry_type, use 'featureUpdate' or 'qualityUpdate'.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"