on":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"Retrieves Windows Update catalog items from Microsoft Intune using the `/deviceManagement/windowsUpdateCatalogItems` endpoint. This data source is used to query available Windows updates with release dates and support lifecycle information.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_windows_updates_compliance_changes":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"compliance_changes":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"content":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"catalog_entry_id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the catalog entry that was approved.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"catalog_entry_type":{"type":"string","description":"The type of catalog entry (featureUpdate, qualityUpdate, driverUpdate).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"The content that was approved for deployment.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"created_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time when the compliance change was created.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"deployment_settings":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"schedule":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"gradual_rollout":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"devices_per_offer":{"type":"number","description":"Number of devices per offer.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"duration_between_offers":{"type":"string","description":"Duration between offers in ISO 8601 format.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Gradual rollout settings.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"start_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time when deployment should start.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Schedule settings for the deployment.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Settings for how the approved content should be deployed.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier for the compliance change.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"is_revoked":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether the compliance change has been revoked.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"revoked_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time when the compliance change was revoked.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"list"},"description":"List of compliance changes (content approvals) for the policy.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update_policy_id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the update policy to query for compliance changes.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"description":"Retrieves compliance changes (content approvals) for a Windows Update policy using the `/admin/windows/updates/updatePolicies/{updatePolicyId}/complianceChanges` endpoint. This data source lists all content approvals that have been created for a policy, including their revocation status and deployment settings.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_windows_updates_device_enrollment":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"device_name":{"type":"string","description":"The device name to search for. The data source will resolve the name to an Entra device ID and then fetch enrollment status. One of `entra_device_id`, `device_name`, or `list_all` must be specified.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"devices":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"enrollments":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"update_category":{"type":"string","description":"The update category the device is enrolled in (feature, quality, driver).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"list"},"description":"List of update management enrollments for this device.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"errors":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"error_code":{"type":"string","description":"The error code.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"error_message":{"type":"string","description":"The error message.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"list"},"description":"List of errors associated with this device's enrollment.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The Entra ID (Azure AD) device object ID.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"list"},"description":"List of enrolled devices with their enrollment status. When querying by `entra_device_id` or `device_name`, this will contain a single device. When using `list_all`, this may contain multiple devices.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"entra_device_id":{"type":"string","description":"The Entra ID (Azure AD) device object ID to query enrollment status for. One of `entra_device_id`, `device_name`, or `list_all` must be specified.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"list_all":{"type":"bool","description":"Set to `true` to list all enrolled devices. Cannot be combined with `entra_device_id` or `device_name`. When using this option, the data source returns all devices in the `devices` attribute. Use `update_category` or `odata_filter` to narrow results.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"odata_filter":{"type":"string","description":"Custom OData filter query for advanced filtering when using `list_all`. Example: `id eq '12345678-1234-1234-1234-123456789012'`. Only applicable when `list_all` is `true`.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update_category":{"type":"string","description":"Optional filter to only return devices enrolled in a specific update category. Valid values: `feature`, `quality`, `driver`. Can be used with any lookup method to filter results.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true}},"description":"Retrieves Windows Autopatch enrollment status for Azure AD devices using the `/admin/windows/updates/updatableAssets` endpoint. This data source supports multiple lookup methods: by Entra device ID, by device name, list all enrolled devices, or use custom OData queries for advanced filtering.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_beta_windows_updates_product":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"products":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"friendly_names":{"type":["list","string"],"description":"The friendly names of the product, e.g., 'Version 22H2 (OS build 22621)'.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"group_name":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the product group, e.g., 'Windows 11'.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier for the product.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"known_issues":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"description":{"type":"string","description":"The description of the known issue.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier for the known issue.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"last_updated_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The last updated date and time of the known issue in RFC3339 format.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"originating_knowledge_base_article":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"id":{"type":"string","description":"The KB article ID.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"url":{"type":"string","description":"The URL to the KB article.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"The KB article that originated the known issue.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"resolved_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The resolved date and time of the known issue in RFC3339 format.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"resolving_knowledge_base_article":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"id":{"type":"string","description":"The KB article ID.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"url":{"type":"string","description":"The URL to the KB article.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"The KB article that resolved the known issue.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"safeguard_hold_ids":{"type":["list","string"],"description":"List of safeguard hold IDs associated with the known issue.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"start_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The start date and time of the known issue in RFC3339 format.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"status":{"type":"string","description":"The status of the known issue.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"title":{"type":"string","description":"The title of the known issue.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"web_view_url":{"type":"string","description":"The URL to view the known issue in the admin portal.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"list"},"description":"Known issues related to the product.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"name":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the product, e.g., 'Windows 11, version 22H2'.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"revisions":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"catalog_entry":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"catalog_name":{"type":"string","description":"The catalog name.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"deployable_until_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The date and time until which the update can be deployed, in RFC3339 format.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"The display name of the catalog entry.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The catalog entry identifier.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"is_expeditable":{"type":"bool","description":"Indicates whether the update can be expedited.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"quality_update_cadence":{"type":"string","description":"The release cadence of the quality update.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"quality_update_classification":{"type":"string","description":"The classification of the quality update.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"release_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The release date and time in RFC3339 format.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"short_name":{"type":"string","description":"The short name of the update.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"The catalog entry associated with this revision.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"The display name of the product revision.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier for the product revision, e.g., '10.0.22621.2215'.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"knowledge_base_article":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"id":{"type":"string","description":"The KB article ID, e.g., 'KB5029351'.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"url":{"type":"string","description":"The URL to the KB article.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"The knowledge base article associated with this revision.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"os_build":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"build_number":{"type":"number","description":"The build number.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"major_version":{"type":"number","description":"The major version number.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"minor_version":{"type":"number","description":"The minor version number.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"update_build_revision":{"type":"number","description":"The update build revision number.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"The OS build information.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"release_date_time":{"type":"string","description":"The release date and time in RFC3339 format.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"version":{"type":"string","description":"The version of the product revision, e.g., '22H2'.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"list"},"description":"Product revisions associated with the search criteria.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"list"},"description":"The list of Windows Update products that match the search criteria.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"search_type":{"type":"string","description":"Type of search to perform. Valid values are: `catalog_id`, `kb_number`.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"search_value":{"type":"string","description":"Value to search by. For catalog_id, provide the catalog identifier. For kb_number, provide the KB article number (e.g., '5029332').","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"Retrieves Windows Update product information from Microsoft Graph. This data source can search by catalog ID or KB number using the `/admin/windows/updates/products/FindByCatalogId` or `/admin/windows/updates/products/FindByKbNumber` endpoints.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_graph_identity_and_access_subscribed_skus":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"account_id":{"type":"string","description":"Filter by account ID (GUID). This typically matches your tenant ID. Conflicts with other lookup attributes.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"account_name":{"type":"string","description":"Filter by account name. Case-insensitive partial match. Conflicts with other lookup attributes.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"applies_to":{"type":"string","description":"Filter by target class. Possible values: 'User', 'Company'. Conflicts with other lookup attributes.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier for this data source operation.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"items":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"account_id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique ID of the account this SKU belongs to.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"account_name":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the account this SKU belongs to.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"applies_to":{"type":"string","description":"The target class for this SKU. Only SKUs with target class 'User' are assignable. Possible values: 'User', 'Company'.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"capability_status":{"type":"string","description":"The status of the SKU. Possible values: 'Enabled', 'Warning', 'Suspended', 'Deleted', 'LockedOut'.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"consumed_units":{"type":"number","description":"The number of licenses that have been assigned.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier for the subscribed SKU object.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"prepaid_units":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"enabled":{"type":"number","description":"The number of units that are enabled.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"locked_out":{"type":"number","description":"The number of units that are locked out.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"suspended":{"type":"number","description":"The number of units that are suspended.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"warning":{"type":"number","description":"The number of units that are in warning state.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Information about the number and status of prepaid licenses.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"service_plans":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"applies_to":{"type":"string","description":"The object the service plan can be assigned to.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"provisioning_status":{"type":"string","description":"The provisioning status of the service plan.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"service_plan_id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier of the service plan.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"service_plan_name":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the service plan.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"list"},"description":"Information about the service plans that are available with the SKU.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"sku_id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier (GUID) for the service SKU.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"sku_part_number":{"type":"string","description":"The SKU part number; for example: 'AAD_PREMIUM' or 'RMSBASIC'.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"subscription_ids":{"type":["list","string"],"description":"A list of all subscription IDs associated with this SKU.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"list"},"description":"List of subscribed SKUs matching the query criteria.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"list_all":{"type":"bool","description":"Retrieve all subscribed SKUs. Conflicts with specific lookup attributes.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"sku_id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier of a specific SKU (format: accountId_skuId). Conflicts with other lookup attributes.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"sku_part_number":{"type":"string","description":"Filter by SKU part number (e.g., 'ENTERPRISEPREMIUM', 'AAD_PREMIUM'). Case-insensitive partial match. Conflicts with other lookup attributes.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"create":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"delete":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Setting a timeout for a Delete operation is only applicable if changes are saved into state before the destroy operation occurs.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours). Read operations occur during any refresh or planning operation when refresh is enabled.","description_kind":"plain","optional":true},"update":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"Retrieves Microsoft 365 license SKUs from Microsoft Entra ID using the `/subscribedSkus` endpoint. Supports flexible lookup by SKU ID, SKU part number, account ID, account name, or applies-to filter.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_utility_deployment_scheduler":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"condition_met":{"type":"bool","description":"Boolean indicating whether all required conditions are satisfied. True means the gate is open and scope IDs are released.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"conditions_detail":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"time_condition_detail":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"condition_met":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether the time condition is satisfied.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"current_time":{"type":"string","description":"The current evaluation time (UTC RFC3339).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"delay_start_time_by":{"type":"number","description":"Required delay in hours from deployment start time.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"deployment_start_time":{"type":"string","description":"The deployment start time used for calculations (UTC RFC3339).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"hours_elapsed":{"type":"number","description":"Hours elapsed since deployment start time.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"required":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether a time condition was specified.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Detailed time condition evaluation.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Detailed breakdown of each condition's evaluation for debugging and monitoring.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"depends_on_scheduler":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"minimum_open_hours":{"type":"number","description":"Minimum number of hours the prerequisite gate must have been open before this gate can open. For example, if set to 48, this gate won't open until 48 hours after the prerequisite gate opened. Must be \u003e= 0.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"prerequisite_delay_start_time_by":{"type":"number","description":"The delay_start_time_by value of the prerequisite scheduler. This is when the prerequisite gate would have opened (hours after deployment_start_time). For example, if Phase 2 has `delay_start_time_by = 168`, set this to 168.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Dependency gate that requires another scheduler to have been open for a minimum duration before this gate can open. Useful for sequential phased rollouts where Phase 3 shouldn't start until Phase 2 has been running successfully for a period. This gate calculates when the prerequisite would have opened and ensures sufficient time has passed.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"deployment_start_time":{"type":"string","description":"The deployment campaign start date and time in UTC (RFC3339 format, e.g., '2024-01-15T00:00:00Z'). All time-based conditions are calculated relative to this timestamp, similar to how Unix epoch time works as a reference point. If not provided, uses the current time on each evaluation (not recommended for time-based conditions). Explicitly setting this value allows coordinating multiple deployment phases to a single campaign start time.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"exclusion_time_windows":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"window":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"date_end":{"type":"string","description":"Absolute end date/time in UTC (RFC3339 format, e.g., '2025-01-05T23:59:59Z'). Use for specific date ranges. If not specified, no end date limit.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"date_start":{"type":"string","description":"Absolute start date/time in UTC (RFC3339 format, e.g., '2024-12-20T00:00:00Z'). Use for specific date ranges like holiday freezes. If not specified, no start date limit.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"days_of_week":{"type":["list","string"],"description":"Days of the week when this window blocks deployment. Valid values: `monday`, `tuesday`, `wednesday`, `thursday`, `friday`, `saturday`, `sunday`. If not specified, all days are included.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"time_of_day_end":{"type":"string","description":"End time in UTC (HH:MM:SS format, e.g., '23:59:59'). If not specified, ends at 23:59:59.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"time_of_day_start":{"type":"string","description":"Start time in UTC (HH:MM:SS format, e.g., '00:00:00'). If not specified, starts at 00:00:00.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"list"},"description":"List of time windows when deployment is blocked.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Defines one or more time windows when the gate must remain closed, even if other conditions are met. Use this for holiday freezes, blackout periods, etc. Exclusions take precedence over inclusions. Multiple windows are evaluated with OR logic (any window matches = deployment blocked).","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier of this deployment scheduler instance.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"inclusion_time_windows":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"window":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"date_end":{"type":"string","description":"Absolute end date/time in UTC (RFC3339 format, e.g., '2024-01-31T23:59:59Z'). Use for specific date ranges. If not specified, no end date limit.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"date_start":{"type":"string","description":"Absolute start date/time in UTC (RFC3339 format, e.g., '2024-01-15T00:00:00Z'). Use for specific date ranges. If not specified, no start date limit.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"days_of_week":{"type":["list","string"],"description":"Days of the week when this window is active. Valid values: `monday`, `tuesday`, `wednesday`, `thursday`, `friday`, `saturday`, `sunday`. If not specified, all days are included.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"time_of_day_end":{"type":"string","description":"End time in UTC (HH:MM:SS format, e.g., '17:00:00'). If not specified, ends at 23:59:59.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"time_of_day_start":{"type":"string","description":"Start time in UTC (HH:MM:SS format, e.g., '09:00:00'). If not specified, starts at 00:00:00.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"list"},"description":"List of time windows when deployment is allowed.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Defines one or more time windows when the gate is allowed to open. The current time must fall within at least one of the defined windows for the gate to open. Use this for office hours restrictions, maintenance windows, etc. Multiple windows are evaluated with OR logic (any window matches = condition passes).","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"manual_override":{"type":"bool","description":"Emergency override to immediately release scope ID(s), bypassing all time conditions and windows. Set to `true` to force-release the gate. Useful for emergency deployments. When enabled, all other conditions are ignored and scope ID(s) are immediately released. Default: false.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"name":{"type":"string","description":"A descriptive name for this deployment phase (e.g., 'Phase 2 - Production Rollout'). Used in status messages.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"released_scope_id":{"type":"string","description":"The single scope ID released by this gate when conditions are met. Returns the value from `scope_id` when the gate opens, or null when conditions are not met. Use this in policy assignments when you provided `scope_id`.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"released_scope_ids":{"type":["list","string"],"description":"List of scope IDs released by this gate when conditions are met. Returns the full `scope_ids` list when the gate opens, or null when conditions are not met. Use this in policy assignments when you provided `scope_ids`.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"require_all_conditions":{"type":"bool","description":"When true, all specified conditions must be met (AND logic). When false, any condition passing will release scope ID(s) (OR logic). Defaults to true. Reserved for future use when multiple condition types are supported.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"scope_id":{"type":"string","description":"A single scope ID (typically a group ID) to release when conditions are met. Use this when deploying to one group. Use either `scope_id` or `scope_ids`, not both.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"scope_ids":{"type":["list","string"],"description":"List of multiple scope IDs (user GUIDs, device GUIDs, etc.) to release when conditions are met. Use this when deploying to multiple individual entities. Use either `scope_id` or `scope_ids`, not both.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"time_condition":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"absolute_earliest":{"type":"string","description":"Absolute earliest time (UTC RFC3339 format) when gate can open, regardless of `delay_start_time_by`. Use this to prevent deployment before a specific date/time (e.g., wait for Patch Tuesday). If specified, gate cannot open before this time even if delay_start_time_by has elapsed.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"absolute_latest":{"type":"string","description":"Absolute deadline (UTC RFC3339 format) when gate must close and will never open again. Use this for time-limited deployment campaigns or change freeze deadlines. If current time exceeds this, gate permanently closes.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"delay_start_time_by":{"type":"number","description":"Number of hours to delay after `deployment_start_time` before allowing the gate to open. Must be \u003e= 0. Set to 0 for immediate release at deployment start time.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"max_open_duration_hours":{"type":"number","description":"Maximum number of hours the gate can remain open after it first opens. Must be \u003e= 0. Use this for pilot/temporary deployments that should automatically expire (e.g., 2-week pilot = 336 hours). When duration expires, gate auto-closes and scope IDs are retracted. Set to 0 for unlimited duration (default behavior).","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Time-based condition that must be satisfied before releasing scope ID(s).","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"A conditional gate valve for phased deployments. Returns scope ID(s) when specified time-based conditions are met, enabling controlled rollout of policies and updates. All times are in UTC (RFC3339 format). When conditions are not met, returns null, preventing deployment to target groups.\n\nThis datasource is evaluated on every Terraform plan/apply, allowing gates to automatically open when conditions are satisfied.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_utility_entra_id_sid_converter":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of this resource.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"object_id":{"type":"string","description":"The Object ID (GUID) in the format `xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx`. Provide this to convert to a SID, or leave empty to convert from a SID.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"sid":{"type":"string","description":"The Security Identifier (SID) in the format `S-1-12-1-\u003crid1\u003e-\u003crid2\u003e-\u003crid3\u003e-\u003crid4\u003e`. Provide this to convert to an Object ID, or leave empty to convert from an Object ID. Each RID component must be a valid 32-bit unsigned integer (0 to 4,294,967,295).","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true,"computed":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"Converts between Microsoft Entra ID Security Identifiers (SIDs) and Object IDs locally using deterministic conversion algorithms. This data source is used for bidirectional SID/GUID conversion in hybrid identity scenarios.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_utility_itunes_app_metadata":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"country_code":{"type":"string","description":"The two-letter country code for the App Store regionto search (e.g., 'us', 'gb', 'jp').","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of this resource.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"results":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"advisories":{"type":["list","string"],"description":"List of content advisories.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"appletv_screenshot_urls":{"type":["list","string"],"description":"List of screenshot URLs for Apple TV.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"artist_id":{"type":"number","description":"The unique identifier for the artist/developer.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"artist_name":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the artist/developer.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"artist_view_url":{"type":"string","description":"The URL to view the artist/developer in the App Store.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"artwork_url_100":{"type":"string","description":"URL for the 100x100 app icon.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"artwork_url_512":{"type":"string","description":"URL for the 512x512 app icon.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"artwork_url_60":{"type":"string","description":"URL for the 60x60 app icon.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"average_rating":{"type":"number","description":"The average user rating of the app.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"average_user_rating_for_current_version":{"type":"number","description":"The average user rating for the current version of the app.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"bundle_id":{"type":"string","description":"The bundle identifier of the app.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"content_advisory_rating":{"type":"string","description":"The content advisory rating (e.g., '4+', '12+', '17+').","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"currency":{"type":"string","description":"The currency code for the price (e.g., 'USD', 'GBP', 'EUR').","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"current_version_release_date":{"type":"string","description":"The release date of the current version.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"description":{"type":"string","description":"The description of the app.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"features":{"type":["list","string"],"description":"List of app features (e.g., 'iosUniversal').","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"file_size_bytes":{"type":"string","description":"The size of the app in bytes.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"formatted_price":{"type":"string","description":"The formatted price of the app (e.g., 'Free', '$0.99').","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"genre_ids":{"type":["list","string"],"description":"List of genre IDs for the app.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"genres":{"type":["list","string"],"description":"List of genres for the app.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"ipad_screenshot_urls":{"type":["list","string"],"description":"List of screenshot URLs for iPad.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"is_game_center_enabled":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether Game Center is enabled for the app.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"is_vpp_device_based_licensed":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether the app supports VPP device-based licensing.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"kind":{"type":"string","description":"The type of content (e.g., 'software').","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"language_codes_iso2a":{"type":["list","string"],"description":"List of supported language codes in ISO 2A format.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"minimum_os_version":{"type":"string","description":"The minimum OS version required to run the app.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"price":{"type":"number","description":"The price of the app in the local currency.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"primary_genre":{"type":"string","description":"The primary genre of the app.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"primary_genre_id":{"type":"number","description":"The ID of the primary genre.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"release_date":{"type":"string","description":"The release date of the app.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"release_notes":{"type":"string","description":"Notes about the latest release of the app.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"screenshot_urls":{"type":["list","string"],"description":"List of screenshot URLs for iPhone.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"seller_name":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the app's seller/developer.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"seller_url":{"type":"string","description":"URL to the seller's website.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"supported_devices":{"type":["list","string"],"description":"List of device models that support the app.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"track_censored_name":{"type":"string","description":"The censored name of the app.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"track_content_rating":{"type":"string","description":"The content rating for the app (e.g., '4+', '12+', '17+').","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"track_id":{"type":"number","description":"The unique identifier for the app.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"track_name":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the app.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"track_view_url":{"type":"string","description":"The URL to view the app in the App Store.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"user_rating_count":{"type":"number","description":"The number of user ratings for the app.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"user_rating_count_for_current_version":{"type":"number","description":"The number of user ratings for the current version of the app.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"version":{"type":"string","description":"The version of the app.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"wrapper_type":{"type":"string","description":"The type of wrapper (e.g., 'software').","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"list"},"description":"The list of app results returned from the iTunes App Store API.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"search_term":{"type":"string","description":"The search term to use when querying the iTunes App Store API.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"Queries iOS and iPadOS app metadata from the iTunes App Store API using the `https://itunes.apple.com/search` endpoint. This data source is used to retrieve bundle IDs, versions, and artwork URLs for VPP app deployment.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_utility_licensing_service_plan_reference":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"guid":{"type":"string","description":"Look up a product by its GUID (exact match). GUIDs are used by the `skuId` property in Microsoft Graph. Example: `\"6fd2c87f-b296-42f0-b197-1e91e994b900\"`.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of this data source operation.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"matching_products":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"guid":{"type":"string","description":"The product GUID used by skuId in Graph API.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"product_name":{"type":"string","description":"The product name as displayed in management portals (e.g., \"Microsoft 365 E3\").","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"service_plans_included":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"guid":{"type":"string","description":"The service plan GUID.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The service plan ID.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"name":{"type":"string","description":"The service plan friendly name.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"list"},"description":"Service plans included in this product.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"string_id":{"type":"string","description":"The product String ID used by PowerShell v1.0 and skuPartNumber in Graph API.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"list"},"description":"List of products matching the search criteria. Populated when searching by product name, string_id, guid, or when searching for service plans (returns products that include the matching service plans).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"matching_service_plans":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"guid":{"type":"string","description":"The service plan GUID.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The service plan ID.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"included_in_skus":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"guid":{"type":"string","description":"The product GUID.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"product_name":{"type":"string","description":"The product name.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"string_id":{"type":"string","description":"The product String ID.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"list"},"description":"List of products (SKUs) that include this service plan.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"name":{"type":"string","description":"The service plan friendly name.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"list"},"description":"List of service plans matching the search criteria. Populated when searching by service plan name, id, or guid. Each entry includes a list of products (SKUs) that include this service plan.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"product_name":{"type":"string","description":"Search for products by name (case-insensitive partial match). Returns all products whose names contain this string. Example: `\"Microsoft 365 E3\"` or `\"Office 365\"`.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"service_plan_guid":{"type":"string","description":"Look up a service plan by its GUID (exact match). Example: `\"113feb6c-3fe4-4440-bddc-54d774bf0318\"`.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"service_plan_id":{"type":"string","description":"Search for service plans by ID (case-insensitive partial match). Returns all service plans whose IDs contain this string. Example: `\"EXCHANGE\"`, `\"TEAMS\"`.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"service_plan_name":{"type":"string","description":"Search for service plans by friendly name (case-insensitive partial match). Returns all service plans whose names contain this string. Example: `\"Exchange Online\"`, `\"Microsoft Teams\"`.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"string_id":{"type":"string","description":"Look up a product by its String ID (exact match, case-insensitive). String IDs are used by PowerShell v1.0 and the `skuPartNumber` property in Microsoft Graph. Example: `\"ENTERPRISEPACK\"`, `\"SPE_E3\"`.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"Queries Microsoft 365 licensing service plan reference data from the embedded licensing database. This data source is used to look up license SKU and service plan GUIDs by human-readable names for assignment configuration.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_utility_macos_pkg_app_metadata":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"installer_file_path_source":{"type":"string","description":"The path to the PKG file to be uploaded. The file must be a valid `.pkg` file. Value is not returned by API call.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"installer_url_source":{"type":"string","description":"The web location of the PKG file, can be a http(s) URL. The file must be a valid `.pkg` file. Value is not returned by API call.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"metadata":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"app_paths":{"type":["list","string"],"description":"List of application paths found in the PKG file.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"cf_bundle_identifier":{"type":"string","description":"The bundle identifier (CFBundleIdentifier) extracted from the PKG file.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"cf_bundle_short_version_string":{"type":"string","description":"The version (CFBundleShortVersionString) extracted from the PKG file.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"included_bundles":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"bundle_id":{"type":"string","description":"The bundle identifier of the included bundle.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"cf_bundle_version":{"type":"string","description":"The CFBundleVersion of the included bundle (may differ from version string).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"path":{"type":"string","description":"The path of the included bundle within the PKG file.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"version":{"type":"string","description":"The version of the included bundle.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"list"},"description":"List of additional bundles included in the PKG file.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"install_location":{"type":"string","description":"The installation location specified in the PKG file.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"md5_checksum":{"type":"string","description":"MD5 hash of the PKG file content as a hexadecimal string.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"min_os_version":{"type":"string","description":"The minimum OS version required by the PKG app.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"name":{"type":"string","description":"The app name extracted from the PKG file.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"package_ids":{"type":["list","string"],"description":"The list of package IDs found in the PKG file.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"sha256_checksum":{"type":"string","description":"SHA256 hash of the PKG file content as a hexadecimal string.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"size_mb":{"type":"number","description":"The size of the PKG file in megabytes (MB).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description":"Extracted metadata from the macOS PKG file.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"Extracts metadata from macOS PKG installer files locally or from URLs. This data source is used to retrieve bundle identifiers, versions, and package details for macOS app deployment.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_utility_microsoft_365_endpoint_reference":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"categories":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"Filter endpoints by network optimization category. Valid values:\n  - `Optimize` - Required endpoints with highest traffic volume, latency sensitive. Direct routing recommended.\n  - `Allow` - Required endpoints with lower traffic volume. Direct routing recommended, proxy acceptable.\n  - `Default` - Optional endpoints or low-priority traffic. Can be routed through proxy.\n\nIf omitted, returns endpoints for all categories. See [Microsoft 365 Network Connectivity Principles](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-365/enterprise/microsoft-365-network-connectivity-principles) for category guidance.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"endpoints":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"category":{"type":"string","description":"Network routing category: `Optimize`, `Allow`, or `Default`. See [Network Connectivity Principles](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-365/enterprise/microsoft-365-network-connectivity-principles).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"express_route":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether this endpoint supports Azure ExpressRoute for Microsoft 365.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"id":{"type":"number","description":"Unique identifier for this endpoint set from Microsoft's service.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"ips":{"type":["list","string"],"description":"List of IP address ranges in CIDR notation (e.g., `40.96.0.0/13`). May be empty for URL-only endpoints.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"notes":{"type":"string","description":"Additional notes about this endpoint from Microsoft, such as third-party services or optional features.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"required":{"type":"bool","description":"Whether this endpoint is required for core Microsoft 365 functionality.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"service_area":{"type":"string","description":"The service area: `MEM`, `Exchange`, `SharePoint`, `Skype`, or `Common`.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"service_area_display_name":{"type":"string","description":"Human-readable display name for the service area.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"tcp_ports":{"type":"string","description":"TCP ports used by this endpoint (comma-separated, e.g., `80,443` or ranges like `1024-65535`).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"udp_ports":{"type":"string","description":"UDP ports used by this endpoint (comma-separated, e.g., `3478-3481`).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"urls":{"type":["list","string"],"description":"List of URL patterns (FQDNs) for this endpoint set. May include wildcards (e.g., `*.office.com`).","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"list"},"description":"List of Microsoft 365 endpoint sets matching the specified filters.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"express_route":{"type":"bool","description":"If `true`, only returns endpoints that support Azure ExpressRoute for Microsoft 365. Useful for organizations using ExpressRoute for optimized connectivity. Defaults to `false` (returns all endpoints regardless of ExpressRoute support).","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of this datasource (format: `{instance}_{hash}`)","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"instance":{"type":"string","description":"The Microsoft 365 cloud instance to query. Valid values:\n  - `worldwide` - Worldwide commercial cloud (including US GCC)\n  - `usgov-dod` - US Government DoD cloud\n  - `usgov-gcchigh` - US Government GCC High cloud\n  - `china` - Microsoft 365 operated by 21Vianet (China)\n\nSee [Microsoft 365 endpoints](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-365/enterprise/microsoft-365-endpoints) for cloud details.","description_kind":"markdown","required":true},"required_only":{"type":"bool","description":"If `true`, only returns endpoints marked as required by Microsoft. Optional endpoints provide enhanced functionality but are not necessary for core service operation. Defaults to `false` (returns all endpoints).","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"service_areas":{"type":["set","string"],"description":"Filter endpoints by service area. Valid values:\n  - `MEM` - Microsoft Endpoint Manager (Intune, Autopilot, Windows Updates)\n  - `Exchange` - Exchange Online and Exchange Online Protection\n  - `SharePoint` - SharePoint Online and OneDrive for Business\n  - `Skype` - Skype for Business Online and Microsoft Teams\n  - `Common` - Microsoft 365 Common (Microsoft Entra ID, Office in browser, etc.)\n\nIf omitted, returns endpoints for all service areas.","description_kind":"markdown","optional":true},"timeouts":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"read":{"type":"string","description":"A string that can be [parsed as a duration](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration) consisting of numbers and unit suffixes, such as \"30s\" or \"2h45m\". Valid time units are \"s\" (seconds), \"m\" (minutes), \"h\" (hours).","description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"nesting_mode":"single"},"description_kind":"plain","optional":true}},"description":"Retrieves Microsoft 365 network endpoints from the official IP Address and URL Web Service using the `https://endpoints.office.com` API. This data source is used to query current IP addresses, URLs, and ports for firewall and proxy configuration.","description_kind":"markdown"}},"microsoft365_utility_microsoft_store_package_manifest_metadata":{"version":0,"block":{"attributes":{"id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of this resource.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"manifests":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"package_identifier":{"type":"string","description":"The package identifier.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"type":{"type":"string","description":"The type identifier for the manifest.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"versions":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"default_locale":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"agreements":{"nested_type":{"attributes":{"agreement":{"type":"string","description":"The agreement text.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"agreement_label":{"type":"string","description":"The agreement label.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"agreement_url":{"type":"string","description":"The agreement URL.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true},"type":{"type":"string","description":"The type identifier for the agreement.","description_kind":"markdown","computed":true}},"nesting_mode":"list"},"description":"List of agreements for the package."